1
00:00:55,888 --> 00:00:56,889
Come on.

2
00:00:57,557 --> 00:00:58,808
Come on!

3
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:10,570
Don't let him get away!

4
00:01:57,575 --> 00:01:58,701
Get inside now!

5
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,953
Hurry up! You're late!

6
00:02:03,456 --> 00:02:05,708
Proxima's gonna have your hide.

7
00:02:06,876 --> 00:02:08,669
Get back in the den.

8
00:02:10,796 --> 00:02:11,922
Look what I stole!

9
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:13,674
Proxima'll give me
an extra portion for this!

10
00:02:13,841 --> 00:02:15,635
Nope, I think she's gonna
give that extra portion to me.

11
00:02:15,801 --> 00:02:16,802
Hey, give it back!

12
00:02:16,886 --> 00:02:17,887
It belongs to
whoever's holding it!

13
00:02:17,970 --> 00:02:18,971
And that's not you!

14
00:02:19,055 --> 00:02:20,056
Lex!

15
00:02:20,514 --> 00:02:21,515
Full Sabacc!

16
00:02:21,682 --> 00:02:22,725
Idiot's Array.

17
00:02:22,808 --> 00:02:23,809
What? Let me see that!

18
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:24,894
Nope, it's my card.

19
00:02:24,977 --> 00:02:26,103
You cheat.

20
00:02:26,937 --> 00:02:27,980
Han!

21
00:02:32,234 --> 00:02:33,402
You were gone too long!

22
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:34,862
I knew something must've
gone wrong.

23
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:36,572
This is nothing.
You should see them.

24
00:02:36,739 --> 00:02:37,990
Look down here!

25
00:02:38,741 --> 00:02:39,950
All right, listen.

26
00:02:40,117 --> 00:02:41,327
I was in the middle
of the exchange,

27
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:42,536
I'm handing over the coaxium

28
00:02:42,703 --> 00:02:44,288
and his goons jumped me,
but I showed 'em.

29
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:45,456
How?

30
00:02:45,539 --> 00:02:46,999
I ran away,
then I boosted their speeder.

31
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:48,167
What, are we going somewhere?

32
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:50,294
Yeah, anywhere we want.

33
00:02:51,128 --> 00:02:53,422
You held on to one of the vials?

34
00:02:53,589 --> 00:02:54,590
Han's back!

35
00:02:57,093 --> 00:02:58,594
This, this is worth...

36
00:02:58,761 --> 00:02:59,845
Five, six hundred credits.

37
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:01,681
That's more than you said
we'd need.

38
00:03:01,847 --> 00:03:03,933
To buy our way out
of the control zone.

39
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,434
And off Corellia.

40
00:03:05,601 --> 00:03:08,688
Han, this could work.

41
00:03:08,854 --> 00:03:09,855
This is gonna work.

42
00:03:10,022 --> 00:03:12,233
Qi'ra, you always said one day
we're gonna get out of here.

43
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,442
This is it.

44
00:03:15,111 --> 00:03:16,737
What are we waiting for?

45
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:24,078
There he is.
Hey, you two!

46
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:27,123
Look who we have here.

47
00:03:27,289 --> 00:03:28,916
Moloch. Hi, how are ya?

48
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,127
I was just on my way
to see Lady Proxima.

49
00:03:32,294 --> 00:03:33,921
You have our money?

50
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:36,340
What a night I had.

51
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:37,967
You're not gonna believe it.
You'll believe it, but...

52
00:03:38,467 --> 00:03:39,468
Search him.

53
00:03:39,885 --> 00:03:41,345
Hold still, scrumrat!

54
00:03:43,556 --> 00:03:44,724
Easy.

55
00:03:45,307 --> 00:03:46,308
Come on.

56
00:03:46,475 --> 00:03:47,727
All right.

57
00:03:48,227 --> 00:03:49,770
Let's go see Lady Proxima.

58
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:13,335
Well, what happened?

59
00:04:13,502 --> 00:04:14,670
I'll tell you what happened.

60
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:16,756
They double-crossed you
and tried to kill me.

61
00:04:16,922 --> 00:04:17,923
The money?

62
00:04:18,048 --> 00:04:20,259
- They kept it.
- And my coaxium?

63
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:22,136
They kept that, too.

64
00:04:22,219 --> 00:04:23,679
But we learned
a very valuable lesson.

65
00:04:23,846 --> 00:04:25,931
We cannot trust those guys.

66
00:04:26,432 --> 00:04:28,100
So you expect me to believe

67
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:30,644
that you walked away
with nothing!

68
00:04:32,521 --> 00:04:34,857
I ran away with my life.
I think that's something.

69
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:36,984
To me, that's a lot.

70
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:39,904
I trusted you
with a simple task,

71
00:04:39,987 --> 00:04:42,156
and all I'm hearing are excuses.

72
00:04:45,284 --> 00:04:48,871
There must be consequences
for disobedience

73
00:04:49,038 --> 00:04:51,415
or else you never learn.

74
00:04:57,671 --> 00:04:58,923
You know what?

75
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:01,926
I don't think
I'm ever gonna learn.

76
00:05:02,092 --> 00:05:03,636
What did you say?

77
00:05:04,261 --> 00:05:07,431
I said, next time
somebody hits me,

78
00:05:08,682 --> 00:05:09,683
I hit 'em back.

79
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,393
Not if I shoot you.

80
00:05:13,437 --> 00:05:14,438
Moloch, wait!

81
00:05:15,064 --> 00:05:16,190
Don't!

82
00:05:16,649 --> 00:05:18,484
Qi'ra, remember the Silo?

83
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:20,653
We pulled you
out of that horror,

84
00:05:20,736 --> 00:05:22,238
gave you a home.

85
00:05:22,404 --> 00:05:25,616
Don't throw it away for Han.
He's not worth it!

86
00:05:25,783 --> 00:05:29,119
Whatever he lost on the deal,
we'll earn it back, double.

87
00:05:29,286 --> 00:05:30,704
We will make it up to you.

88
00:05:30,996 --> 00:05:32,456
Coaxium is precious.

89
00:05:32,873 --> 00:05:34,208
Scrumrats like you come cheap.

90
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,336
Everybody, stand back!

91
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:38,754
What's that supposed to be?

92
00:05:38,921 --> 00:05:40,673
This is a thermal detonator

93
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,716
that I just armed.

94
00:05:42,883 --> 00:05:45,386
- That's a rock!
- No, it's not.

95
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:46,637
Yes, it is!

96
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:47,972
And you just made

97
00:05:48,055 --> 00:05:49,348
a clicking sound
with your mouth.

98
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:51,016
Please tell me
this isn't your plan.

99
00:05:51,183 --> 00:05:52,518
No, this is.

100
00:06:02,903 --> 00:06:04,071
- Get in!
- An M-68?

101
00:06:04,238 --> 00:06:06,240
- Nice, right?
- I love it!

102
00:06:39,231 --> 00:06:41,775
There's a starliner leaving
from Coronet Spaceport,

103
00:06:41,859 --> 00:06:43,110
we're gonna be on it.

104
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,072
We bribe our way through the
checkpoint, and we're free.

105
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:49,909
I'm gonna be a pilot.

106
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:51,368
We can get our own ship.

107
00:06:51,535 --> 00:06:53,287
See the galaxy, all of it.

108
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:57,666
We won't have to take orders
or be kicked around by anyone.

109
00:06:58,709 --> 00:06:59,710
Ever.

110
00:07:03,255 --> 00:07:05,049
Thought we'd get
a little more of a head start.

111
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:23,400
Hang on!

112
00:07:32,868 --> 00:07:34,536
This is a secure area.

113
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:36,413
You must have proper clearance.

114
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:39,166
Stop at once!
You must follow the proper...

115
00:07:40,417 --> 00:07:41,418
Protocol.

116
00:07:44,588 --> 00:07:46,423
Damn! That stinger's fast.

117
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:49,093
Yeah, but we're faster, right?

118
00:07:49,259 --> 00:07:50,344
I hope so.

119
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:21,750
Pull over!

120
00:08:43,939 --> 00:08:44,940
Han, no,
we're not gonna make it!

121
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:46,025
Yeah?

122
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:47,568
Han, I'm telling you,
it's too tight!

123
00:08:48,193 --> 00:08:49,194
Watch this.

124
00:09:09,298 --> 00:09:10,591
Bring the hounds.

125
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,551
After them!

126
00:09:13,594 --> 00:09:14,595
Come on!

127
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:16,847
We gotta move.

128
00:09:28,358 --> 00:09:29,651
Do not join the line

129
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:31,904
if you don't have
a boarding pass.

130
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:35,741
No access without ID chip.

131
00:09:36,241 --> 00:09:39,036
All droids must be registered.

132
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:42,331
Move along. Move along.

133
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,877
Stand down. Do not resist!

134
00:09:48,253 --> 00:09:49,755
- Stop struggling.
- Let me go!

135
00:09:49,838 --> 00:09:50,839
Take his arm.

136
00:09:51,006 --> 00:09:52,049
I got him.

137
00:09:52,132 --> 00:09:53,133
Take him to cell 3B.

138
00:09:53,842 --> 00:09:54,843
This way, come on.

139
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:57,679
Keep moving. Hold it, hold it.

140
00:09:59,681 --> 00:10:01,016
Next.

141
00:10:05,187 --> 00:10:06,897
Han, they're here.

142
00:10:09,608 --> 00:10:10,609
Hey, what are you...

143
00:10:10,692 --> 00:10:13,737
We're almost there.

144
00:10:13,904 --> 00:10:15,197
- Just hold on to me.
- Next.

145
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:16,573
Don't look back.

146
00:10:17,741 --> 00:10:19,743
Once we're through,
we've gotta be smart,

147
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:21,411
figure out where we're going.

148
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:23,664
Anywhere the Empire isn't.
Wherever we go,

149
00:10:23,747 --> 00:10:25,249
it can't be worse
than where we've been.

150
00:10:25,415 --> 00:10:28,627
Yes, it can. Out there,
we've got no protection.

151
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:30,879
We could get snatched up
by traffickers,

152
00:10:30,963 --> 00:10:33,382
sold to Crimson Dawn
or the Hutt Cartel.

153
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:35,092
That's not gonna happen.

154
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:36,635
I won't let it.

155
00:10:44,601 --> 00:10:45,644
For luck?

156
00:10:46,645 --> 00:10:47,938
Damn right.

157
00:10:51,775 --> 00:10:53,110
You heard him. Let's go.

158
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,278
Next.

159
00:10:57,197 --> 00:10:58,282
ID chips.

160
00:10:58,657 --> 00:11:00,826
Funny thing, we don't have 'em.

161
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:01,994
We have this.

162
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:03,370
Refined hyperfuel.

163
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:06,790
It's worth at least
800 credits, maybe more.

164
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,877
You could be detained
just for having that.

165
00:11:10,210 --> 00:11:11,920
What good would that do anybody?

166
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:13,881
Let us through, it's all yours.

167
00:11:23,765 --> 00:11:25,642
The coaxium, now.

168
00:11:25,809 --> 00:11:27,519
As we're going through,
not before.

169
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:33,734
Do it.

170
00:11:35,986 --> 00:11:37,112
Just do it, do it.

171
00:11:41,283 --> 00:11:43,202
Not so fast, Qi'ra! Come on!

172
00:11:43,869 --> 00:11:45,329
Wait!
Open the door!

173
00:11:45,495 --> 00:11:47,164
Security! Security,
there has been a breach!

174
00:11:48,123 --> 00:11:49,416
Open the door!

175
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:51,668
- Run! Run!
- Get your hands off of her!

176
00:11:51,752 --> 00:11:52,753
Run!

177
00:11:53,253 --> 00:11:54,796
Get your hands off of her!

178
00:11:55,547 --> 00:11:56,673
Qi'ra!

179
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:59,176
Run, Han! Go!

180
00:11:59,426 --> 00:12:00,677
Keep moving.

181
00:12:02,804 --> 00:12:03,847
Qi'ra!

182
00:12:04,014 --> 00:12:05,015
Run!

183
00:12:05,098 --> 00:12:06,099
Traveler has been apprehended.

184
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:09,853
Qi'ra, I'll come back!
I'll come back!

185
00:12:12,814 --> 00:12:13,857
All units,
there has been a breach.

186
00:12:14,566 --> 00:12:17,486
Another unauthorized traveler
made it through the gate.

187
00:12:18,278 --> 00:12:19,738
One got through
the gate! Look over there!

188
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:21,740
Someone
got through the checkpoint.

189
00:12:29,706 --> 00:12:31,875
- Keep an eye on that gate.
- Yes, sir.

190
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:33,210
Can't let you through
without a ticket.

191
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:35,128
Can't let you through
without a ticket.

192
00:12:36,171 --> 00:12:37,297
Hey, wait!

193
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:39,299
- Hey!
- Come with us.

194
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:43,637
He's still
out there. Keep looking.

195
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:57,192
You there, stop!

196
00:12:57,359 --> 00:12:59,236
- Show me some identification.
- Please. Please. No, no!

197
00:12:59,861 --> 00:13:00,946
Do not resist.

198
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:04,491
Be a part of
something. Join the Empire.

199
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:08,495
Explore new worlds.
Learn valuable skills.

200
00:13:09,037 --> 00:13:11,999
Bring order and unity
to the galaxy!

201
00:13:12,874 --> 00:13:15,711
Be a part of something.
Join the Empire.

202
00:13:17,546 --> 00:13:19,506
This is where I sign up
to be a pilot, right?

203
00:13:19,673 --> 00:13:20,841
If you apply
for the Imperial Navy,

204
00:13:20,924 --> 00:13:22,592
but most recruits
go into the infantry.

205
00:13:22,759 --> 00:13:25,971
I'm gonna be a pilot.
Best in the galaxy.

206
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:27,681
You there, come with us.

207
00:13:27,764 --> 00:13:28,807
Who, me?

208
00:13:28,890 --> 00:13:30,434
We have a few questions
to ask you.

209
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,477
How long is that gonna take?

210
00:13:32,644 --> 00:13:34,813
Depends on how good you are
at following orders.

211
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,440
Why, have you got
somewhere to be?

212
00:13:36,606 --> 00:13:38,400
Yeah, back here,
as soon as I can.

213
00:13:39,651 --> 00:13:42,696
Don't hear that much.
What's your name, son?

214
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:44,114
Han.

215
00:13:44,614 --> 00:13:45,991
Han what?

216
00:13:47,576 --> 00:13:48,577
Who are your people?

217
00:13:52,664 --> 00:13:55,417
I don't have people.
I'm alone.

218
00:13:56,626 --> 00:13:57,627
Han...

219
00:14:00,756 --> 00:14:01,798
Solo.

220
00:14:03,342 --> 00:14:04,343
Approved.

221
00:14:04,843 --> 00:14:08,513
Proceed to transport ID 83 for
the Naval Academy at Carida.

222
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:11,099
Good luck, Han Solo.

223
00:14:11,266 --> 00:14:13,685
We'll have you flying
in no time.

224
00:14:26,239 --> 00:14:29,701
Your Empire needs you.
Troopers forward!

225
00:14:30,118 --> 00:14:31,536
Solo, get up!
We're almost there!

226
00:14:31,953 --> 00:14:34,539
Almost where?
Where are we going?

227
00:14:34,706 --> 00:14:37,417
Just over that last ridge.
Victory is...

228
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:51,515
My legs! My leg!

229
00:15:06,738 --> 00:15:08,490
Hey, Beckett,
you said we were here

230
00:15:08,573 --> 00:15:09,658
to pull a quick job.

231
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:11,743
- Yeah.
- Well, this ain't a quick job!

232
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:13,203
It's a war!

233
00:15:14,037 --> 00:15:15,831
It's always something with you.

234
00:15:17,416 --> 00:15:19,501
AT-hauler.
That's what we came for.

235
00:15:20,335 --> 00:15:22,754
Forward operations
must be this way.

236
00:15:22,921 --> 00:15:25,215
They are, but the major said
we're supposed to go that way!

237
00:15:25,382 --> 00:15:27,175
Yeah, go that way and die!

238
00:15:27,342 --> 00:15:29,553
That's exactly what happened
to the major!

239
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:32,097
Who's the ranking officer now?

240
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:34,057
You are, Captain.

241
00:15:36,059 --> 00:15:37,561
He's got you there.

242
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:41,606
So what's the plan,
Captain Beckett?

243
00:15:41,773 --> 00:15:45,026
Val, you take Rio and these
four mud skulls flank left.

244
00:15:45,193 --> 00:15:46,987
I'll take this mouthy scooch

245
00:15:47,070 --> 00:15:49,156
and we'll go around to the right

246
00:15:49,322 --> 00:15:50,407
and maybe we'll get lucky.

247
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:52,033
Luck's got
nothin' to do with it.

248
00:15:52,868 --> 00:15:54,494
Wait! One question!

249
00:15:55,203 --> 00:15:57,205
- You wanna live, sparky?
- Very much.

250
00:15:57,372 --> 00:15:59,499
Then shut up and do what
your captain tells you.

251
00:16:00,625 --> 00:16:02,043
Let's go!

252
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:17,476
Captain.

253
00:16:17,642 --> 00:16:19,394
T-15s are down.
We walk from here.

254
00:16:19,561 --> 00:16:20,896
Captain.

255
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:24,149
I'm Han.

256
00:16:25,358 --> 00:16:26,651
Nobody cares.

257
00:16:28,361 --> 00:16:30,155
Thanks for your help back there.

258
00:16:30,322 --> 00:16:31,531
You did all right.

259
00:16:32,365 --> 00:16:34,159
I was trained
in aerial combat...

260
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:36,036
You want some advice?

261
00:16:36,203 --> 00:16:37,537
Get the hell away from here.

262
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:40,165
Any way you can,
as fast as you can.

263
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:44,836
What company do you command?

264
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,338
None of your business company.

265
00:16:46,505 --> 00:16:48,298
And we're full up.

266
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:50,342
Stick to soldiering, kid.

267
00:16:50,425 --> 00:16:52,052
You don't want any part of this.

268
00:16:58,475 --> 00:16:59,726
Hang on, guys!

269
00:17:01,895 --> 00:17:03,313
Attention!

270
00:17:03,688 --> 00:17:06,399
In three hours, we move out
for the southern marshlands.

271
00:17:06,566 --> 00:17:09,027
I want an advance party
of ten men.

272
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:10,820
Great, more mud.

273
00:17:11,154 --> 00:17:12,572
What was that?

274
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:15,825
Just wondering what our
objective is, Lieutenant.

275
00:17:16,284 --> 00:17:18,954
Bring peace and prosperity
to the galaxy,

276
00:17:19,120 --> 00:17:20,872
install a regime
loyal to the Emperor,

277
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:22,374
and eradicate the hostiles.

278
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:25,210
It's their planet,
we're the hostiles.

279
00:17:26,044 --> 00:17:27,712
You got a problem, trooper?

280
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,257
No problem, sir.

281
00:17:33,009 --> 00:17:34,135
Moving out.

282
00:17:34,302 --> 00:17:36,888
To the southern
marshlands! Move out!

283
00:17:37,055 --> 00:17:39,224
You heard 'em!
Let's move out!

284
00:17:48,191 --> 00:17:49,693
Looks like
they're running sorties

285
00:17:49,776 --> 00:17:50,777
every 30 minutes.

286
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:53,196
Yeah, I can take out the
guards at the perimeter,

287
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:54,823
signalman, pilot.

288
00:17:54,906 --> 00:17:56,366
Hell, I'll just
take 'em all out.

289
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:57,826
What are we looking at?

290
00:18:01,454 --> 00:18:03,456
You have a talent for
sticking your nose in

291
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:04,708
where it doesn't belong.

292
00:18:04,874 --> 00:18:06,042
I just couldn't help but notice

293
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:08,587
you're wearing a uniform
pock-full of laser burns.

294
00:18:08,753 --> 00:18:10,630
So either you heal real quick

295
00:18:10,714 --> 00:18:13,341
or you stole it off a dead man.

296
00:18:13,508 --> 00:18:14,843
You're not Imperial Army.

297
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:17,304
You're thieves here
to steal equipment

298
00:18:17,387 --> 00:18:18,722
for a job and I want in.

299
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:21,641
- Well, now we gotta shoot him.
- No.

300
00:18:22,475 --> 00:18:24,436
Snap his neck. It's less mess.

301
00:18:24,603 --> 00:18:25,770
Or you take me with you.

302
00:18:25,937 --> 00:18:28,523
Look, I came up running scams
on the streets of Corellia.

303
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:31,067
I was boosting AV-21 s
when I was ten.

304
00:18:31,151 --> 00:18:32,819
I'm a driver, a flyer,

305
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:36,531
and hey, you said yourself.
I gotta get outta here. Right?

306
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:38,742
What's a fancy flyboy
doing down in the mud?

307
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:42,245
I got kicked out
of the Imperial Academy

308
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:43,830
for having a mind of my own.

309
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:47,250
But I am a great pilot.
And I gotta get home.

310
00:18:47,667 --> 00:18:49,878
This guy is nuts.
No one goes back to Corellia.

311
00:18:50,045 --> 00:18:51,504
I got a reason.

312
00:18:51,671 --> 00:18:53,757
We've already got a great pilot.

313
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:56,384
The Ardennian.

314
00:18:56,551 --> 00:18:58,470
Ardennian?
You got a lot of nerve, pal.

315
00:18:58,553 --> 00:19:00,221
I'm an imperial trooper.

316
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:01,306
Really?
A couple of your arms

317
00:19:01,389 --> 00:19:02,390
popped out of your butt

318
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:03,850
and hiked up your pants,
trooper.

319
00:19:03,933 --> 00:19:04,934
Yeah?

320
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:07,062
Look, I'll do whatever it
takes to get back to Corellia.

321
00:19:07,228 --> 00:19:08,897
I've already been away too long.

322
00:19:09,564 --> 00:19:10,565
Just give me a shot.

323
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:11,941
Hold it.

324
00:19:14,235 --> 00:19:15,695
Well, if you're
not interested in me,

325
00:19:15,862 --> 00:19:18,990
I think the lieutenant might
be very interested in you.

326
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:23,745
Blackmail.

327
00:19:26,122 --> 00:19:27,123
Lieutenant.

328
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:28,208
Captain.

329
00:19:29,084 --> 00:19:31,252
Lieutenant, we have
apprehended a deserter.

330
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:32,379
Take him.

331
00:19:32,545 --> 00:19:33,546
Wait.

332
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:36,049
I should've known.
This one's a troublemaker.

333
00:19:36,424 --> 00:19:37,425
And a liar.

334
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:38,551
Don't believe anything he says.

335
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:40,679
- Don't go anywhere without me.
- All right, let's go.

336
00:19:40,845 --> 00:19:42,055
Feed him to the beast.

337
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:43,682
The beast?
Wait, there's a beast?

338
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:44,766
- Hold on!
- Move it!

339
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:46,976
Listen, that guy's not
even an officer. All right?

340
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:48,436
- He was lying!
- Quiet!

341
00:19:50,814 --> 00:19:51,815
Don't care.

342
00:19:54,192 --> 00:19:55,902
Haven't fed him in three days.

343
00:19:56,069 --> 00:19:57,153
Should be fun.

344
00:20:44,367 --> 00:20:46,661
Hey!
Hey, big fella.

345
00:20:46,828 --> 00:20:49,414
Just calm down.
Take it easy.

346
00:20:49,706 --> 00:20:50,874
We're on the same side.

347
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:52,250
You like treats?

348
00:20:54,002 --> 00:20:56,337
Help!
Let me out of here!

349
00:20:56,504 --> 00:20:57,714
Let me out of here!

350
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:03,219
Gotcha!

351
00:21:23,823 --> 00:21:25,241
This was just getting good.

352
00:21:25,408 --> 00:21:26,951
- He killed him too fast.
- Yeah!

353
00:21:27,118 --> 00:21:28,411
Kill him slower.

354
00:21:31,122 --> 00:21:32,665
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

355
00:21:32,832 --> 00:21:35,126
Wait! Wait!

356
00:21:39,005 --> 00:21:40,131
Yeah, I speak a little.

357
00:21:40,215 --> 00:21:41,341
Now just listen to me, you...

358
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:42,675
You dumb Wookiee!

359
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:50,225
Me have plan of break out.

360
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:54,521
You and I freedom make...
by secret battle of pretend.

361
00:21:55,939 --> 00:21:58,733
Look... big... stick...

362
00:22:01,736 --> 00:22:03,238
Yes, yes!

363
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:05,698
No, no, no, no!

364
00:22:07,992 --> 00:22:08,993
Do it!

365
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:10,537
Come on.

366
00:22:12,455 --> 00:22:13,832
No!

367
00:22:13,998 --> 00:22:16,000
Ten credits, he doesn't
last another minute.

368
00:22:16,167 --> 00:22:17,877
Let me out of here!

369
00:22:18,044 --> 00:22:19,420
I can't take it anymore!

370
00:22:20,922 --> 00:22:22,549
- No! Stop, please!
- That's it. Get him!

371
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:27,262
You tired, you mangy
Kashyyykian moof-milker?

372
00:22:39,023 --> 00:22:41,484
See what happens
when you listen to me?

373
00:22:41,776 --> 00:22:43,486
Hey, what are you doing?

374
00:22:50,493 --> 00:22:51,494
Follow me!

375
00:23:02,338 --> 00:23:03,840
Wait, wait.

376
00:23:04,007 --> 00:23:05,592
Come here.
Listen to me.

377
00:23:05,758 --> 00:23:06,759
You don't understand, okay?

378
00:23:06,843 --> 00:23:07,844
I have some very good friends

379
00:23:07,927 --> 00:23:08,970
waiting for me at that airfield.

380
00:23:09,053 --> 00:23:10,388
They're leaving right now.

381
00:23:10,555 --> 00:23:12,015
That's our one way
off this mud ball.

382
00:23:12,181 --> 00:23:13,766
If you wanna live,
we go that way.

383
00:23:13,933 --> 00:23:16,144
After that, you go whichever
way you want, I don't care!

384
00:23:16,311 --> 00:23:18,396
But right now,
that's the way you go!

385
00:23:20,773 --> 00:23:22,108
Trust me!

386
00:23:22,901 --> 00:23:25,528
Val, let's go!

387
00:23:28,406 --> 00:23:30,700
How do they breathe in these
suits? It's so stuffy!

388
00:23:31,576 --> 00:23:33,411
No wonder
they're such lousy pilots.

389
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:35,079
You can't turn your head,
you can't breathe,

390
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:36,164
you can't hear each other!

391
00:23:43,379 --> 00:23:44,756
I'll be damned.

392
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:46,257
Hey, look who's back!

393
00:23:46,424 --> 00:23:47,508
Unbelievable!

394
00:23:47,675 --> 00:23:49,302
Wait!

395
00:23:49,469 --> 00:23:51,137
Wait!

396
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:54,057
Is that a Wookiee?
Incredible!

397
00:23:54,223 --> 00:23:55,391
I'll say it, I don't care.

398
00:23:55,558 --> 00:23:57,101
This kid's growing on me.

399
00:23:57,310 --> 00:23:59,103
Wait!

400
00:24:03,024 --> 00:24:04,192
You know, we could always use

401
00:24:04,275 --> 00:24:05,318
some muscle on a job like this.

402
00:24:05,902 --> 00:24:07,695
Don't even think about it!

403
00:24:07,862 --> 00:24:10,365
I'm telling you, you will
never have a deeper sleep

404
00:24:10,531 --> 00:24:12,116
than curled up
in a Wookiee's lap.

405
00:24:17,830 --> 00:24:20,458
I told you!

406
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:22,627
Very good friends!

407
00:24:47,986 --> 00:24:50,613
We couldn't have done this
maybe, like, one at a time?

408
00:25:18,599 --> 00:25:20,560
Thanks for helping me
get outta there.

409
00:25:26,566 --> 00:25:28,693
No, they only took you
because of me.

410
00:25:29,569 --> 00:25:30,570
Hey!

411
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:33,531
I got us a real sweet deal here.

412
00:25:33,698 --> 00:25:35,658
We do this one job with them,

413
00:25:35,825 --> 00:25:37,702
we make some real money,

414
00:25:37,869 --> 00:25:39,704
and then we're free.

415
00:25:39,871 --> 00:25:41,956
When's the last time
you could say that?

416
00:25:45,418 --> 00:25:47,670
Been a while for me, too.

417
00:25:49,088 --> 00:25:51,257
So what's your name, anyway?

418
00:25:54,677 --> 00:25:56,471
Chewbacca?

419
00:25:57,221 --> 00:25:59,557
All right, well, you're gonna
need a nickname,

420
00:25:59,724 --> 00:26:01,642
'cause I ain't saying that
every time.

421
00:26:06,856 --> 00:26:07,899
Here it comes.
Take a look.

422
00:26:07,982 --> 00:26:08,983
Yeah.

423
00:26:09,150 --> 00:26:12,695
We hit the Conveyex between
the tower and the bridge.

424
00:26:13,112 --> 00:26:16,407
Rio drops us in, we separate
the payload container,

425
00:26:16,574 --> 00:26:19,035
cable it up to the AT-hauler
and then...

426
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:20,828
Rio jams their distress signal.

427
00:26:21,662 --> 00:26:22,955
I blow the bridge,

428
00:26:23,039 --> 00:26:24,582
the container slides
right off the track

429
00:26:24,749 --> 00:26:25,958
and we sail away.

430
00:26:26,125 --> 00:26:27,877
You trip that security beam,

431
00:26:28,044 --> 00:26:29,295
wake up those Vipers,

432
00:26:29,378 --> 00:26:31,380
it's liable to get
real spicy, real fast.

433
00:26:31,547 --> 00:26:33,466
Well, I'm not the one
you should be worried about.

434
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:34,884
Enfys Nest.

435
00:26:35,051 --> 00:26:36,636
What's an Enfys Nest?

436
00:26:36,803 --> 00:26:38,054
I told you, we're way ahead

437
00:26:38,137 --> 00:26:39,514
of the competition on this one.

438
00:26:39,680 --> 00:26:41,057
There's no way Enfys Nest

439
00:26:41,140 --> 00:26:43,059
even knows about this shipment.

440
00:26:43,226 --> 00:26:44,727
Only my guy has the intel.

441
00:26:44,894 --> 00:26:47,355
Well, you better be right.
Yeah?

442
00:26:47,522 --> 00:26:49,732
Because sometimes,
you put your faith

443
00:26:49,816 --> 00:26:51,359
in the wrong people.

444
00:26:53,236 --> 00:26:55,655
Our whole future
depends on this one score

445
00:26:55,822 --> 00:26:57,073
and you bring in amateurs.

446
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,449
In case you hadn't noticed,

447
00:26:58,533 --> 00:26:59,742
we're a little shorthanded.

448
00:27:00,284 --> 00:27:01,285
So we get who we need.

449
00:27:01,452 --> 00:27:03,955
The Xan sisters, or Bossk.

450
00:27:04,122 --> 00:27:06,666
But, no, instead you're
putting our lives

451
00:27:06,749 --> 00:27:08,126
in the hands of morons.

452
00:27:09,127 --> 00:27:10,336
You guys morons?

453
00:27:10,503 --> 00:27:11,671
No!

454
00:27:11,838 --> 00:27:13,381
- No. See?
- We're not morons.

455
00:27:13,548 --> 00:27:16,384
Look, I waited a long time
for a shot like this.

456
00:27:16,551 --> 00:27:18,553
I'm not about to screw it up,
all right?

457
00:27:19,137 --> 00:27:20,138
Come on, Val!

458
00:27:20,304 --> 00:27:21,848
He looks so sincere.

459
00:27:22,014 --> 00:27:23,474
Plus, have you ever
tried to disinvite

460
00:27:23,558 --> 00:27:24,642
a Wookiee to anything?

461
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:26,602
Not a good idea!

462
00:27:27,270 --> 00:27:28,604
This is not funny!

463
00:27:28,813 --> 00:27:33,067
Look, now, I have great
instincts about these guys.

464
00:27:33,234 --> 00:27:36,863
And, besides,
do you see any other options?

465
00:27:37,029 --> 00:27:38,281
I just hope you know
what you're doing.

466
00:27:38,447 --> 00:27:41,075
Yeah, I know exactly
what I'm doing and why.

467
00:27:41,242 --> 00:27:42,910
We're gonna clear our debts,

468
00:27:43,077 --> 00:27:45,079
go back to Glee Anselm,

469
00:27:45,872 --> 00:27:48,499
and I'm finally gonna learn
how to play that valachord.

470
00:27:48,666 --> 00:27:51,127
Babe, you're never gonna learn
how to play the valachord.

471
00:27:51,294 --> 00:27:53,087
She's right.
You are tone-deaf.

472
00:27:56,299 --> 00:27:58,467
So what's your sob story,
flyboy?

473
00:27:58,634 --> 00:27:59,635
Who, me?

474
00:27:59,802 --> 00:28:01,679
You're after something,
I know the look.

475
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:03,514
What is it?
Revenge?

476
00:28:04,307 --> 00:28:05,975
No, it's not revenge.

477
00:28:06,142 --> 00:28:07,351
Look at him.

478
00:28:07,518 --> 00:28:09,020
If it's anything, it's a girl.

479
00:28:09,103 --> 00:28:10,146
A girl!

480
00:28:10,229 --> 00:28:12,648
Tell us about the girl, Han.
Is she nice?

481
00:28:13,482 --> 00:28:14,984
Does she have sharp teeth?

482
00:28:18,237 --> 00:28:19,447
There was a girl.

483
00:28:21,866 --> 00:28:23,576
But I got out, she didn't.

484
00:28:25,119 --> 00:28:27,997
I swore to myself
I'd become a pilot,

485
00:28:28,164 --> 00:28:29,707
get a ship,

486
00:28:29,874 --> 00:28:31,167
go back and find her.

487
00:28:32,501 --> 00:28:35,838
That's what I'm gonna do
right after this job.

488
00:28:36,005 --> 00:28:38,257
How you know
she'll still be there?

489
00:28:39,217 --> 00:28:40,259
I just know.

490
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:42,511
Personally, I refuse
to be tied down

491
00:28:42,595 --> 00:28:44,347
by anyone,
though many have tried.

492
00:28:44,513 --> 00:28:47,016
Come on, Rio.
You don't fool me.

493
00:28:47,391 --> 00:28:49,393
Everybody needs somebody.

494
00:28:50,102 --> 00:28:53,814
Even a broken down
old crook like this one.

495
00:29:04,533 --> 00:29:06,535
How about you? What are you
gonna do with your share?

496
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:20,758
What was he saying?

497
00:29:20,925 --> 00:29:22,385
He said the Wookiees
were enslaved

498
00:29:22,468 --> 00:29:24,387
by the Empire,
taken off Kashyyyk.

499
00:29:24,553 --> 00:29:27,306
He's searching for his...

500
00:29:28,015 --> 00:29:30,351
I don't know if he said
tribe or family.

501
00:29:31,560 --> 00:29:32,687
What's the difference?

502
00:29:35,898 --> 00:29:37,149
Show me how to do that.

503
00:29:37,650 --> 00:29:39,777
The only thing
you need to learn to do

504
00:29:42,530 --> 00:29:44,949
is do what I say when I say it.

505
00:29:45,574 --> 00:29:46,867
And this time tomorrow,

506
00:29:47,451 --> 00:29:48,744
you'll have more than enough

507
00:29:48,911 --> 00:29:50,538
to buy your own ship.

508
00:30:11,726 --> 00:30:13,227
Starting the clock.

509
00:30:13,394 --> 00:30:15,771
Jamming their signal.
9.6 to the bridge.

510
00:30:15,938 --> 00:30:18,566
Let's find out how good
we really are, folks.

511
00:30:30,036 --> 00:30:31,037
I'm fine!

512
00:30:35,333 --> 00:30:36,792
Val, how's it going up there?

513
00:30:41,047 --> 00:30:42,548
Never better.

514
00:31:05,529 --> 00:31:07,031
Coaxium.

515
00:31:07,198 --> 00:31:09,200
Enough to power a fleet!

516
00:31:09,367 --> 00:31:11,494
Or blow us all straight to hell!

517
00:31:14,455 --> 00:31:15,498
All right, talk to me.

518
00:31:15,998 --> 00:31:17,083
Is it a good day?

519
00:31:17,458 --> 00:31:18,751
It's a great day!

520
00:31:18,918 --> 00:31:21,504
Best day of your life,
my grabby friend!

521
00:31:21,670 --> 00:31:22,963
I don't know, you've never been

522
00:31:23,047 --> 00:31:24,423
to a Mynock roast on Ardennia.

523
00:31:24,590 --> 00:31:25,674
It's nuts!

524
00:31:28,344 --> 00:31:29,428
Here they come!

525
00:31:29,595 --> 00:31:31,138
Get down to the couplers!

526
00:31:31,305 --> 00:31:32,932
Rio, fall back!

527
00:31:33,099 --> 00:31:34,183
Well, that didn't take 'em long.

528
00:31:52,576 --> 00:31:53,744
Chewie!

529
00:32:09,802 --> 00:32:11,429
You all right?

530
00:32:11,595 --> 00:32:13,389
Little close there, buddy!

531
00:32:18,018 --> 00:32:19,562
Han, what's the holdup?

532
00:32:20,646 --> 00:32:21,856
All right, together.

533
00:32:24,150 --> 00:32:25,151
Now!

534
00:32:31,365 --> 00:32:32,616
All right!

535
00:32:38,581 --> 00:32:40,875
They got one uncoupled.
Where are you, buddy?

536
00:32:41,041 --> 00:32:43,210
Just up here
planning my retirement.

537
00:32:43,377 --> 00:32:44,420
Thinking about opening a cantina

538
00:32:44,503 --> 00:32:46,046
somewhere warm
but not too warm, you know?

539
00:32:46,213 --> 00:32:48,716
Lowering the winch cables now!

540
00:33:06,066 --> 00:33:07,943
I knew it! I told him!
Beckett!

541
00:33:08,110 --> 00:33:09,487
He's coming!

542
00:33:10,446 --> 00:33:13,157
Damn it! I'm never gonna
hear the end of this!

543
00:33:17,870 --> 00:33:18,954
Who's that?

544
00:33:19,121 --> 00:33:20,456
Enfys Nest!

545
00:33:20,623 --> 00:33:22,374
Marauders, pirates.

546
00:33:22,541 --> 00:33:24,210
Come to snake the score
from under us.

547
00:33:25,294 --> 00:33:26,795
Ready your harpoons.

548
00:33:26,962 --> 00:33:28,172
Move in.

549
00:34:08,337 --> 00:34:10,673
Hang on!
I got an uninvited guest.

550
00:34:10,839 --> 00:34:14,385
Get off of my ship!

551
00:34:18,472 --> 00:34:20,474
You still with us, brother?

552
00:34:20,641 --> 00:34:22,142
Yeah, I'm okay.

553
00:34:22,309 --> 00:34:24,478
Just nicked one of my
shoulders. It's nothing.

554
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:26,105
He's not okay.

555
00:34:33,195 --> 00:34:34,238
Chewie!

556
00:34:34,905 --> 00:34:37,199
You gotta uncouple this one
on your own!

557
00:34:42,955 --> 00:34:44,164
Han!

558
00:34:44,331 --> 00:34:45,499
I'm on it!

559
00:34:55,134 --> 00:34:56,135
Val!

560
00:34:56,302 --> 00:34:59,054
Keep your eyes open.
We just tripped a sensor.

561
00:35:04,393 --> 00:35:06,186
Viper droids headed your way!

562
00:35:07,354 --> 00:35:09,231
Rio?

563
00:35:09,398 --> 00:35:11,150
Yeah, it looks worse than it is.

564
00:35:11,900 --> 00:35:13,402
Just gotta patch it up.

565
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:16,614
Maybe rest my eyes for a minute.

566
00:35:36,925 --> 00:35:38,719
Enough!
I'm going in.

567
00:36:04,119 --> 00:36:05,663
You weren't lying, kid.

568
00:36:06,830 --> 00:36:08,207
You're a hell of a pilot.

569
00:36:08,374 --> 00:36:10,417
Rio, stay with me, buddy.

570
00:36:22,971 --> 00:36:25,015
Beckett, we just lost a cable!

571
00:36:26,058 --> 00:36:28,102
2. 1 to the bridge!

572
00:36:32,106 --> 00:36:33,691
It's no good to die alone, kid.

573
00:36:35,234 --> 00:36:36,568
Val was right.

574
00:36:39,196 --> 00:36:40,280
Rio?

575
00:37:11,186 --> 00:37:12,730
Beckett, we're .8
from the bridge!

576
00:37:12,896 --> 00:37:14,940
Val's still on the track!

577
00:37:15,107 --> 00:37:17,109
Val, you gotta
get off that bridge!

578
00:37:17,276 --> 00:37:18,360
We're here!

579
00:37:22,614 --> 00:37:24,074
They got me pinned!

580
00:37:24,366 --> 00:37:26,535
I'm gonna have to finish
the job from right here.

581
00:37:26,785 --> 00:37:27,953
What?

582
00:37:28,245 --> 00:37:30,247
It's been a ride, babe.

583
00:37:31,623 --> 00:37:33,792
And I wouldn't trade it
for anything.

584
00:37:34,209 --> 00:37:35,210
Val!

585
00:37:35,294 --> 00:37:36,295
No!

586
00:37:41,967 --> 00:37:44,386
No!

587
00:37:57,983 --> 00:37:59,610
Chewie, now!

588
00:38:22,674 --> 00:38:24,718
Beckett, I can't
pull it away from 'em.

589
00:38:25,135 --> 00:38:27,554
They'll let go,
you fly straight!

590
00:38:29,807 --> 00:38:31,141
Release your cables

591
00:38:31,517 --> 00:38:32,810
or die!

592
00:38:34,061 --> 00:38:35,062
We're too close.

593
00:38:35,229 --> 00:38:36,230
I gotta release.

594
00:38:36,396 --> 00:38:37,648
You do what I tell you, Han!

595
00:38:37,815 --> 00:38:38,857
Chewie, grab the line!

596
00:38:39,024 --> 00:38:40,275
Don't you do it!

597
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:44,738
Han!

598
00:38:44,905 --> 00:38:46,448
You coward!

599
00:39:35,414 --> 00:39:36,874
What the hell?

600
00:39:37,040 --> 00:39:40,127
You don't listen
and you can't follow orders!

601
00:39:40,294 --> 00:39:42,713
You have any idea
what you've done?

602
00:39:42,880 --> 00:39:45,507
We were not stealing
for ourselves,

603
00:39:45,674 --> 00:39:48,260
we were hired by Crimson Dawn.

604
00:39:50,804 --> 00:39:52,723
Crimson Dawn?

605
00:39:52,890 --> 00:39:55,142
Now we owe them 100 keys
of refined coaxium.

606
00:39:55,309 --> 00:39:57,603
When they find out
we don't got it,

607
00:39:57,769 --> 00:39:59,521
they're gonna kill us.

608
00:40:00,772 --> 00:40:02,482
Right.

609
00:40:02,649 --> 00:40:03,650
We run.

610
00:40:03,817 --> 00:40:06,820
I'm already a deserter.
What's the difference?

611
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:07,905
The difference

612
00:40:08,071 --> 00:40:09,740
is the Empire doesn't send out

613
00:40:09,823 --> 00:40:11,825
a team of enforcers
to hunt you down

614
00:40:11,992 --> 00:40:13,368
when you're a deserter.

615
00:40:13,535 --> 00:40:15,078
Dryden Vos will.

616
00:40:17,122 --> 00:40:18,457
You have any idea what it's like

617
00:40:18,540 --> 00:40:20,667
to live with a price
on your head?

618
00:40:21,585 --> 00:40:24,171
The only thing to do
is to go to them.

619
00:40:24,379 --> 00:40:26,965
Maybe I can find some way
to make it up to him.

620
00:40:31,345 --> 00:40:33,013
Then that's what we do.

621
00:40:37,559 --> 00:40:38,769
No.

622
00:40:42,856 --> 00:40:45,192
He knows me, not you.

623
00:40:46,318 --> 00:40:48,654
If you come with me

624
00:40:49,279 --> 00:40:51,239
and show your face,

625
00:40:51,615 --> 00:40:53,659
if they don't kill you,

626
00:40:54,910 --> 00:40:57,037
you're in this life for good.

627
00:40:59,331 --> 00:41:02,167
You find some way
to square this,

628
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:05,921
we still get our money?

629
00:41:07,839 --> 00:41:09,424
Maybe.

630
00:41:11,718 --> 00:41:14,262
For me, it's worth the risk.

631
00:41:16,598 --> 00:41:17,808
How about you?

632
00:41:24,606 --> 00:41:26,274
That's yes.

633
00:41:28,485 --> 00:41:31,571
Sorry I punched your face.

634
00:41:31,738 --> 00:41:34,324
Happens more often
than you think.

635
00:41:35,993 --> 00:41:37,160
So when we get up there,

636
00:41:37,244 --> 00:41:39,204
Dryden Vos is waiting for us
at Fort Ypso?

637
00:41:39,371 --> 00:41:41,873
Nearby, on his yacht.

638
00:41:42,416 --> 00:41:44,292
You're gonna know
how to find it?

639
00:41:44,459 --> 00:41:46,420
That won't be a problem.

640
00:42:27,544 --> 00:42:29,588
I'll need to check your weapons.

641
00:42:31,465 --> 00:42:32,632
That's all I got left.

642
00:43:09,336 --> 00:43:13,006
Welcome back, Tobias Beckett.

643
00:43:13,507 --> 00:43:16,343
I'm here to see
Dryden. He's expecting me.

644
00:43:16,510 --> 00:43:17,886
He'll be with you shortly.

645
00:43:18,345 --> 00:43:19,846
He's just finishing
with the regional governor.

646
00:43:25,185 --> 00:43:26,436
Excuse me, sir.

647
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:27,521
Yes.

648
00:43:27,604 --> 00:43:30,315
Beckett has arrived.

649
00:43:32,484 --> 00:43:36,071
Put this in my office.
I might be needing it later.

650
00:43:42,702 --> 00:43:45,330
I get all worked up.
Silly.

651
00:43:45,497 --> 00:43:46,790
It's a party.

652
00:43:50,293 --> 00:43:51,378
Hey.

653
00:43:51,962 --> 00:43:54,422
These people are
not your friends

654
00:43:54,589 --> 00:43:57,300
and they're never gonna be,
so don't talk to any of 'em.

655
00:43:57,467 --> 00:43:58,677
Don't look at anybody,

656
00:43:58,844 --> 00:44:00,554
just keep your eyes down.

657
00:44:04,182 --> 00:44:05,600
I might get a drink.

658
00:44:18,655 --> 00:44:19,906
No, yeah, whatever.

659
00:44:38,425 --> 00:44:40,886
Chewie, would you please...

660
00:44:49,853 --> 00:44:51,479
Qi'ra, what are you doing here?

661
00:44:51,646 --> 00:44:53,106
I work here.

662
00:44:53,273 --> 00:44:54,900
What's your excuse?

663
00:44:55,066 --> 00:44:56,401
My... I...

664
00:44:56,568 --> 00:44:58,236
Qi'ra, I was...

665
00:45:00,363 --> 00:45:02,657
I was coming back for you.

666
00:45:03,491 --> 00:45:05,202
It's in the past, Han.

667
00:45:05,285 --> 00:45:06,286
Not for me.

668
00:45:06,369 --> 00:45:07,412
The only reason I'm here,

669
00:45:07,495 --> 00:45:08,496
I was doing this job,
get a little money

670
00:45:08,663 --> 00:45:10,874
and then I was gonna come back
to Corellia and find you.

671
00:45:11,333 --> 00:45:13,627
Well, now you don't have to.

672
00:45:14,419 --> 00:45:16,379
I'm right in front of you.

673
00:45:18,632 --> 00:45:19,841
That day...

674
00:45:20,008 --> 00:45:21,593
Sometimes,
a lot of times, I think...

675
00:45:21,760 --> 00:45:23,011
If you'd have stayed,

676
00:45:24,137 --> 00:45:26,223
they would've killed you.

677
00:45:27,682 --> 00:45:29,893
I'm glad you got out.

678
00:45:33,939 --> 00:45:35,523
How did you get out?

679
00:45:39,194 --> 00:45:41,071
I didn't.

680
00:45:44,241 --> 00:45:45,492
You look good.

681
00:45:46,034 --> 00:45:47,327
A little rough around the edges,

682
00:45:47,744 --> 00:45:49,246
but good.

683
00:45:49,746 --> 00:45:51,039
You too.

684
00:45:51,623 --> 00:45:52,791
Thank you, Ottilie.

685
00:45:53,792 --> 00:45:55,252
Have you been attentive
to Dok-Ondar?

686
00:45:55,418 --> 00:45:56,503
Very.

687
00:46:00,423 --> 00:46:01,716
What should we drink to?

688
00:46:02,509 --> 00:46:05,345
Let's drink two
and see where it goes.

689
00:46:13,270 --> 00:46:15,939
Did you ever get that ship
we were going to fly away on?

690
00:46:16,106 --> 00:46:18,024
Yeah.
Sort of.

691
00:46:18,191 --> 00:46:20,235
About to.
That's why I'm here.

692
00:46:20,402 --> 00:46:22,612
I'm working on a...

693
00:46:22,779 --> 00:46:24,531
Very big deal.

694
00:46:24,698 --> 00:46:25,949
How big?

695
00:46:26,032 --> 00:46:27,033
Enormous.

696
00:46:27,117 --> 00:46:30,412
Really? And when are you going
to close this enormous deal?

697
00:46:30,578 --> 00:46:32,163
Any minute.

698
00:46:33,665 --> 00:46:35,750
I thought about you a lot.

699
00:46:35,917 --> 00:46:39,170
Off somewhere, some adventure.

700
00:46:39,337 --> 00:46:42,757
I imagined myself with you.
It always made me...

701
00:46:45,385 --> 00:46:46,928
- What?
- Hey.

702
00:46:47,178 --> 00:46:48,346
What did I say?

703
00:46:49,264 --> 00:46:51,433
Look, I can't keep my eyes
down the whole time.

704
00:46:51,599 --> 00:46:52,851
I'm gonna bump into something.

705
00:46:53,018 --> 00:46:54,060
But I told you
not to talk to anyone.

706
00:46:54,144 --> 00:46:55,145
Beckett.

707
00:46:56,313 --> 00:46:59,190
Wait.
You two work together?

708
00:47:00,233 --> 00:47:01,735
- Yeah.
- Tobias!

709
00:47:03,445 --> 00:47:04,821
Dryden.

710
00:47:05,030 --> 00:47:07,157
Are you all right?
Are you hurt?

711
00:47:07,324 --> 00:47:09,200
No, I'm fine.

712
00:47:10,118 --> 00:47:11,703
I'm sorry to hear about Val.

713
00:47:11,870 --> 00:47:12,912
Yeah, I appreciate that.

714
00:47:13,079 --> 00:47:14,581
But there was no way
we could've anticipated...

715
00:47:14,748 --> 00:47:17,167
I don't believe
we've been introduced.

716
00:47:17,334 --> 00:47:20,211
Yeah. This is Han Solo
and Chewbacca.

717
00:47:20,378 --> 00:47:21,796
They're with me.

718
00:47:21,963 --> 00:47:23,590
I'm Dryden Vos.

719
00:47:23,757 --> 00:47:27,135
I see you've already met my
top lieutenant.

720
00:47:29,804 --> 00:47:31,890
Han and I grew up
together on Corellia.

721
00:47:32,682 --> 00:47:34,100
Fellow scrumrat.

722
00:47:35,143 --> 00:47:38,188
I admire anyone who can crawl
their way out of the sewer.

723
00:47:38,730 --> 00:47:41,274
Especially,
a sewer as putrid as Corellia.

724
00:47:41,483 --> 00:47:43,777
The stench, am I right?

725
00:47:44,861 --> 00:47:45,987
Well, it's good to have you.

726
00:47:46,196 --> 00:47:47,822
Welcome.

727
00:47:47,989 --> 00:47:50,241
And you, too, Chewbacca,
welcome.

728
00:47:51,451 --> 00:47:54,954
All right, let's eat a little,
drink a lot,

729
00:47:55,121 --> 00:47:56,748
and talk privately.

730
00:47:59,542 --> 00:48:01,336
We're just friends, all right?

731
00:48:01,419 --> 00:48:03,421
You're touchy.

732
00:48:04,047 --> 00:48:07,467
Beckett, you have
put me in a terrible position.

733
00:48:07,634 --> 00:48:09,594
I know, Dryden, and I am sorry.

734
00:48:09,677 --> 00:48:10,720
You're sorry?

735
00:48:10,804 --> 00:48:11,805
Dryden,
there were complications.

736
00:48:11,888 --> 00:48:12,889
There were factors.

737
00:48:12,972 --> 00:48:16,309
Enfys Nest has been
a constant irritation forever.

738
00:48:16,476 --> 00:48:18,019
It's one you should've
anticipated,

739
00:48:18,186 --> 00:48:19,646
it's one you should've
dealt with.

740
00:48:19,813 --> 00:48:21,106
Trust me, I know
I made a mistake,

741
00:48:21,272 --> 00:48:22,941
but when you hired me,
you told me

742
00:48:23,024 --> 00:48:24,734
no one else
had this information...

743
00:48:24,901 --> 00:48:26,694
Test me!

744
00:48:27,487 --> 00:48:30,281
Test me one more time,
you'll see what happens.

745
00:48:30,448 --> 00:48:32,575
I think what Dryden
is trying to say

746
00:48:32,742 --> 00:48:35,412
is that we're not interested
in why you don't have it.

747
00:48:35,912 --> 00:48:37,705
No, I'm not interested.

748
00:48:37,872 --> 00:48:39,499
I'm not interested at all.

749
00:48:39,666 --> 00:48:40,667
Dryden,

750
00:48:40,959 --> 00:48:43,128
what can I do
to make this right?

751
00:48:43,420 --> 00:48:44,921
"Make this right?"

752
00:48:45,088 --> 00:48:47,340
There is no making this right.

753
00:48:47,507 --> 00:48:48,758
You know who I answer to

754
00:48:48,925 --> 00:48:50,969
and you know
what he'll expect of me.

755
00:48:51,136 --> 00:48:53,888
He'll say, "There have to be
consequences."

756
00:48:54,055 --> 00:48:56,558
So here's what I need you
to do for me.

757
00:48:57,058 --> 00:49:00,603
I need you to give me a reason

758
00:49:00,770 --> 00:49:03,523
not to kill you all.

759
00:49:03,690 --> 00:49:05,775
Because I will
make it up to you.

760
00:49:05,859 --> 00:49:06,943
No, no, no. How?

761
00:49:07,110 --> 00:49:08,778
How will you make it up to me?

762
00:49:08,945 --> 00:49:11,823
By delivering exactly
what was promised.

763
00:49:12,365 --> 00:49:15,326
100 k-grams of refined coaxium?

764
00:49:15,493 --> 00:49:18,746
Yes. We will simply steal it
from somewhere else.

765
00:49:18,913 --> 00:49:20,206
From where?

766
00:49:20,373 --> 00:49:21,666
You'll be hard pushed
to find that

767
00:49:21,749 --> 00:49:22,959
anywhere outside
an Imperial vault.

768
00:49:23,126 --> 00:49:25,003
Scarif. Maybe Mercy Island.

769
00:49:25,170 --> 00:49:26,463
That's impossible.

770
00:49:26,629 --> 00:49:29,007
So, let's come up
with some other options.

771
00:49:29,174 --> 00:49:30,425
Other ideas that we might...

772
00:49:30,592 --> 00:49:32,510
What about unrefined?

773
00:49:35,805 --> 00:49:38,683
Well, the only known
source of astatic coaxium

774
00:49:38,850 --> 00:49:41,478
is a fissure vent beneath
the spice mines on Kessel.

775
00:49:41,644 --> 00:49:43,771
Yeah. That's the one
I was thinking of.

776
00:49:43,938 --> 00:49:45,648
That's a very, very good one.

777
00:49:45,815 --> 00:49:48,109
But see,
the Pykes control Kessel.

778
00:49:48,610 --> 00:49:49,611
Crimson Dawn maintains

779
00:49:49,694 --> 00:49:51,154
a fragile alliance
with the Pykes.

780
00:49:51,321 --> 00:49:53,531
It's one that I can't jeopardize

781
00:49:53,698 --> 00:49:55,909
without risking an all-out
war with the Syndicates,

782
00:49:56,075 --> 00:49:58,953
and that, gentlemen,
I will not do.

783
00:49:59,120 --> 00:50:02,624
So, if that's all you have,
I think we're done here.

784
00:50:02,749 --> 00:50:03,791
Not all we have.

785
00:50:03,875 --> 00:50:06,377
We don't have any alliance
with the Pykes.

786
00:50:06,544 --> 00:50:09,214
Right, so nobody is gonna know
we're working for you.

787
00:50:18,806 --> 00:50:19,807
Possible?

788
00:50:20,475 --> 00:50:21,726
It's risky.

789
00:50:21,893 --> 00:50:24,103
As soon as the raw coaxium
is removed from the vault,

790
00:50:24,270 --> 00:50:25,813
it starts to destabilize,

791
00:50:25,980 --> 00:50:27,649
so unless...

792
00:50:27,815 --> 00:50:29,234
Unless...

793
00:50:29,400 --> 00:50:30,652
Unless...

794
00:50:31,528 --> 00:50:32,529
Work with me here.

795
00:50:32,695 --> 00:50:34,364
Unless you could find somewhere

796
00:50:34,447 --> 00:50:36,032
to get it processed fast.

797
00:50:38,201 --> 00:50:39,911
Well...

798
00:50:40,537 --> 00:50:41,663
He's saying Savareen?

799
00:50:41,829 --> 00:50:43,289
Savareen.

800
00:50:43,456 --> 00:50:45,458
Yeah, it's an old refinery there

801
00:50:45,625 --> 00:50:47,252
and it's not under
Imperial jurisdiction.

802
00:50:47,418 --> 00:50:48,461
But Qi'ra's right.

803
00:50:49,087 --> 00:50:52,048
The canisters will explode
before you get there,

804
00:50:52,549 --> 00:50:55,176
so you'd need
an incredibly fast ship

805
00:50:55,260 --> 00:50:56,594
and a brilliant pilot.

806
00:50:56,803 --> 00:50:58,221
We'll find a ship.

807
00:50:58,388 --> 00:51:00,139
We've already got the pilot.

808
00:51:04,727 --> 00:51:07,981
He is arrogant and he's hungry.

809
00:51:08,523 --> 00:51:10,275
So what do you think, my dear?

810
00:51:10,441 --> 00:51:14,946
You think your friend here
can do what needs to be done?

811
00:51:20,868 --> 00:51:23,037
Yes, I believe he can.

812
00:51:24,414 --> 00:51:25,957
Well, that is good news,

813
00:51:26,040 --> 00:51:27,625
because you're going with him

814
00:51:28,084 --> 00:51:30,545
to see that he does.

815
00:51:31,629 --> 00:51:33,506
All right?

816
00:51:34,716 --> 00:51:35,925
Of course.

817
00:51:37,427 --> 00:51:38,845
All right.

818
00:51:39,012 --> 00:51:40,388
I'll see you all on Savareen.

819
00:51:40,555 --> 00:51:41,639
Savareen it is.

820
00:51:41,806 --> 00:51:43,433
- I feel great about this plan.
- Me, too.

821
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:45,226
We should do this again.
It's been fun.

822
00:51:45,643 --> 00:51:46,644
Great.

823
00:51:46,811 --> 00:51:48,146
Just one more thing.

824
00:51:48,313 --> 00:51:50,273
If you do fail me again,

825
00:51:52,025 --> 00:51:53,651
we'll all be out of options.

826
00:51:53,943 --> 00:51:54,944
Right?

827
00:51:55,028 --> 00:51:56,321
We won't.

828
00:51:59,365 --> 00:52:01,284
So, I thought
that went really well.

829
00:52:02,327 --> 00:52:04,579
Let's get this done as quick
and as clean as possible.

830
00:52:04,662 --> 00:52:05,663
What do you need?

831
00:52:05,747 --> 00:52:07,081
I can scrounge up the gear.

832
00:52:07,248 --> 00:52:08,541
Do you got a line on a ship?

833
00:52:08,708 --> 00:52:09,959
I know a guy.

834
00:52:11,169 --> 00:52:12,920
And I know
just where to find him.

835
00:52:13,671 --> 00:52:15,673
It's a long shot,
but it's worth a try.

836
00:52:15,840 --> 00:52:17,008
He's the best smuggler around.

837
00:52:17,175 --> 00:52:18,593
He's slipped through
the Empire's fingers

838
00:52:18,676 --> 00:52:20,345
more times than anyone else.

839
00:52:20,845 --> 00:52:23,014
He's attractive, too.

840
00:52:23,181 --> 00:52:24,223
Sophisticated,

841
00:52:24,390 --> 00:52:28,394
with impeccable taste
and... Charisma.

842
00:52:29,812 --> 00:52:31,773
Not to mention his prodigious...

843
00:52:31,939 --> 00:52:32,940
We get it.

844
00:52:37,904 --> 00:52:40,782
But he's retired.
Says he's a sportsman now.

845
00:52:40,948 --> 00:52:42,575
All we need is his ship.

846
00:52:42,742 --> 00:52:44,243
Well, he'll never part with it.

847
00:52:44,410 --> 00:52:45,578
He loves that ship.

848
00:52:45,745 --> 00:52:47,246
He won it

849
00:52:47,914 --> 00:52:49,082
playing Sabacc.

850
00:52:49,165 --> 00:52:50,166
And there's the rub, right?

851
00:52:50,249 --> 00:52:52,085
How was I supposed to know
she was an Imperial spy?

852
00:52:52,251 --> 00:52:54,587
I thought she loved me.

853
00:52:54,671 --> 00:52:56,089
That's the guy?

854
00:52:57,757 --> 00:52:59,217
An interesting style.

855
00:52:59,384 --> 00:53:00,385
I'll say.

856
00:53:01,469 --> 00:53:02,804
You say he won his ship?

857
00:53:02,970 --> 00:53:04,597
You have an awful Sabacc face.
I'm gonna call it.

858
00:53:04,764 --> 00:53:05,973
I can take him.
Let me at him.

859
00:53:06,140 --> 00:53:07,475
Absolutely not.

860
00:53:07,642 --> 00:53:09,894
Han, these guys
are serious gamblers.

861
00:53:10,061 --> 00:53:11,729
I'm serious. Stake me.

862
00:53:12,355 --> 00:53:14,440
Don't listen to him.

863
00:53:20,947 --> 00:53:22,865
Thank you. Thank you.

864
00:53:23,032 --> 00:53:24,701
You see, how'd you guys
let me beat you on that one?

865
00:53:24,867 --> 00:53:26,077
Come on.

866
00:53:27,161 --> 00:53:29,038
There's no liars in this game,
just players.

867
00:53:29,205 --> 00:53:31,082
Is this seat taken?

868
00:53:33,751 --> 00:53:36,212
If nobody's in the seat,
then it ain't taken, friend.

869
00:53:39,298 --> 00:53:41,926
So this is Sabacc?

870
00:53:42,009 --> 00:53:43,010
Sabacc.

871
00:53:43,094 --> 00:53:45,388
Sabacc. Got it.

872
00:53:45,555 --> 00:53:46,556
You play it before?

873
00:53:46,973 --> 00:53:48,349
A couple times, yeah.

874
00:53:50,226 --> 00:53:51,394
Captain Lando Calrissian.

875
00:53:51,561 --> 00:53:52,562
Han Solo.

876
00:53:53,396 --> 00:53:55,189
Looks like you're
having a good day.

877
00:53:55,356 --> 00:53:56,399
I'm a lucky guy.

878
00:53:57,734 --> 00:54:00,403
Can I ask you a question,
Captain Calrissian?

879
00:54:00,570 --> 00:54:01,821
Anything, Han.

880
00:54:01,988 --> 00:54:04,949
That's "Han", but that's okay.

881
00:54:05,616 --> 00:54:09,454
I heard a story about you.
I was wondering if it's true.

882
00:54:10,705 --> 00:54:14,000
Everything you've
heard about me is true.

883
00:54:14,083 --> 00:54:15,168
Thanks, love.

884
00:54:15,251 --> 00:54:17,170
Did you win your ship
playing cards?

885
00:54:17,628 --> 00:54:19,714
I've won a lot of things.

886
00:54:20,715 --> 00:54:23,801
I once won a subtropical moon
in the Oseon Belt.

887
00:54:25,428 --> 00:54:26,846
Turned out to be
a real money pit.

888
00:54:26,929 --> 00:54:27,930
I'm impressed.

889
00:54:28,014 --> 00:54:29,390
I don't think I'd have
the nerve to gamble

890
00:54:29,474 --> 00:54:31,058
with something
I love as much as my ship.

891
00:54:31,225 --> 00:54:32,852
- Really?
- Yeah.

892
00:54:33,019 --> 00:54:34,061
What do you fly?

893
00:54:34,979 --> 00:54:36,773
VCX-100.

894
00:54:38,274 --> 00:54:40,318
That is a quality ship.
Right, boys?

895
00:54:40,485 --> 00:54:42,111
It's the fastest in the galaxy,

896
00:54:42,278 --> 00:54:43,780
but there's a lot of
great ships out there.

897
00:54:43,946 --> 00:54:45,823
I mean, I'm sure
yours is very nice.

898
00:54:45,990 --> 00:54:47,867
Gets me where I'm goin'.

899
00:54:52,371 --> 00:54:53,498
Beginner's luck.

900
00:54:53,664 --> 00:54:55,458
Well played.

901
00:55:02,924 --> 00:55:04,801
Let's see what we got here.

902
00:55:04,967 --> 00:55:06,135
Great hand!

903
00:55:10,431 --> 00:55:13,392
Sorry, guys.
Close, but not quite.

904
00:55:22,819 --> 00:55:24,987
Eyes on your own cards, buddy.

905
00:55:25,696 --> 00:55:27,281
All of 'em.

906
00:55:27,448 --> 00:55:28,991
There. Well, now I see yours.

907
00:55:34,372 --> 00:55:38,793
That's me?
Okay, let's see...

908
00:55:41,254 --> 00:55:43,047
Sorry, minus two.

909
00:55:47,844 --> 00:55:49,095
This game is fun.

910
00:55:49,679 --> 00:55:51,097
All right, how about this?

911
00:55:51,764 --> 00:55:54,600
I'll see your bet
and I'll raise you.

912
00:55:55,852 --> 00:55:57,979
2,000.

913
00:56:01,732 --> 00:56:03,109
I'll see your 2,000

914
00:56:03,693 --> 00:56:05,695
and I'll raise you

915
00:56:05,862 --> 00:56:08,197
however much this is.

916
00:56:10,783 --> 00:56:12,410
Han.

917
00:56:12,577 --> 00:56:13,953
Slow down.

918
00:56:14,120 --> 00:56:15,329
You might wanna quit
while you're ahead.

919
00:56:15,663 --> 00:56:17,874
You might wanna quit
while you're behind.

920
00:56:19,959 --> 00:56:21,627
I like this kid.

921
00:56:21,711 --> 00:56:22,753
You're adorable.

922
00:56:22,837 --> 00:56:23,963
And I'm serious.

923
00:56:24,463 --> 00:56:25,798
And I'm calling.

924
00:56:26,215 --> 00:56:27,300
With what?

925
00:56:27,466 --> 00:56:28,551
Your scarf?

926
00:56:28,718 --> 00:56:29,802
Not my style.

927
00:56:29,969 --> 00:56:31,304
My ship.

928
00:56:32,388 --> 00:56:33,973
Against your ship.

929
00:56:35,766 --> 00:56:37,810
Time to find out
if you got the nerve.

930
00:56:40,646 --> 00:56:41,898
What the hell?

931
00:56:45,818 --> 00:56:47,069
Straight Staves.

932
00:56:57,288 --> 00:56:59,457
You played me.
You're good.

933
00:56:59,624 --> 00:57:01,417
- Yeah.
- You're very good.

934
00:57:01,584 --> 00:57:03,210
But not good enough.

935
00:57:03,377 --> 00:57:04,754
Full Sabacc.

936
00:57:11,385 --> 00:57:13,387
I told you to quit
while you were ahead.

937
00:57:15,097 --> 00:57:17,099
Drinks on me!

938
00:57:21,312 --> 00:57:22,688
Yeah, that's right.

939
00:57:30,071 --> 00:57:31,280
First of all, there's no way

940
00:57:31,364 --> 00:57:32,740
he could've had
that green sylop.

941
00:57:32,907 --> 00:57:34,033
They'd all been played.

942
00:57:34,200 --> 00:57:35,660
Also, your guy,
Captain Wonderful,

943
00:57:35,743 --> 00:57:36,953
is so full of bantha crap...

944
00:57:37,119 --> 00:57:38,871
Yoo-hoo!

945
00:57:40,706 --> 00:57:42,541
Where's my VCX?

946
00:57:43,417 --> 00:57:44,669
I don't have it right here now.

947
00:57:44,752 --> 00:57:46,003
It's in the shop.

948
00:57:46,170 --> 00:57:48,339
- I'm getting some work done.
- Lando.

949
00:57:49,674 --> 00:57:51,133
Qi'ra.

950
00:57:52,218 --> 00:57:55,179
You look phenomenal.
As always.

951
00:57:55,346 --> 00:57:57,223
Well, I knew I was
gonna see you.

952
00:57:57,848 --> 00:57:58,891
Get off!

953
00:57:58,975 --> 00:58:00,267
What are you doing
with hairy and the boy?

954
00:58:00,434 --> 00:58:02,561
- There's no need, none.
- They work for me.

955
00:58:02,937 --> 00:58:04,271
Good help is hard to find, no?

956
00:58:04,438 --> 00:58:05,982
We're more like partners.

957
00:58:06,691 --> 00:58:07,984
We are.

958
00:58:08,067 --> 00:58:09,068
Excuse us.

959
00:58:10,152 --> 00:58:11,612
Listen, last I checked,

960
00:58:11,779 --> 00:58:13,197
me and Crimson Dawn,
we're squared away.

961
00:58:13,364 --> 00:58:15,241
Dryden said all is forgiven

962
00:58:15,324 --> 00:58:17,201
after I did the whole
Felucia thing for him.

963
00:58:17,368 --> 00:58:20,371
Yeah. New move,
we're making the Kessel Run.

964
00:58:21,747 --> 00:58:22,915
We need a ship.

965
00:58:23,082 --> 00:58:24,250
Why didn't you just say so?

966
00:58:24,417 --> 00:58:25,710
I thought you were retired.

967
00:58:26,877 --> 00:58:28,796
Circumstances change.

968
00:58:29,338 --> 00:58:30,756
How much?

969
00:58:30,923 --> 00:58:32,341
The Kessel Run.

970
00:58:32,508 --> 00:58:35,136
That's no easy spin.
I'm gonna need half the take.

971
00:58:35,302 --> 00:58:37,013
Ridiculous.

972
00:58:37,096 --> 00:58:38,764
Grown-ups are talking.

973
00:58:38,931 --> 00:58:40,349
25%.

974
00:58:45,604 --> 00:58:46,939
You're Tobias Beckett.

975
00:58:47,648 --> 00:58:48,816
You killed Aurra Sing.

976
00:58:50,359 --> 00:58:52,653
Pushed her. Pretty sure
the fall killed her.

977
00:58:52,820 --> 00:58:55,656
You did the galaxy a favor
that day. Me, especially.

978
00:58:55,823 --> 00:58:57,033
I owed her a lot of money.

979
00:58:57,116 --> 00:58:58,784
And as token of my gratitude,

980
00:58:59,243 --> 00:59:01,537
I'm willing to do this for 40%.

981
00:59:04,790 --> 00:59:06,459
25.

982
00:59:11,380 --> 00:59:13,090
25% works.

983
00:59:13,382 --> 00:59:15,676
No! Unacceptable!

984
00:59:15,843 --> 00:59:18,262
Stop exploiting droids!

985
00:59:18,429 --> 00:59:20,097
You sloppy degenerate bios!

986
00:59:20,264 --> 00:59:21,766
- She never learns.
- Have you no shame?

987
00:59:21,849 --> 00:59:22,850
Who?

988
00:59:23,017 --> 00:59:24,226
My first mate.

989
00:59:24,393 --> 00:59:26,020
You got no business
being here. Get out of here!

990
00:59:26,187 --> 00:59:29,231
How can you condone
this savagery?

991
00:59:29,398 --> 00:59:31,776
You, you.
You should not be doing this.

992
00:59:31,942 --> 00:59:34,070
They're using you
for entertainment.

993
00:59:34,653 --> 00:59:36,322
Yeah.
You've been neurowashed.

994
00:59:36,489 --> 00:59:38,657
Don't just blindly
follow the program.

995
00:59:38,824 --> 00:59:40,743
Exercise some free will!

996
00:59:41,869 --> 00:59:43,245
Stay away from him!

997
00:59:43,412 --> 00:59:44,997
He's never had it so good.

998
00:59:45,164 --> 00:59:47,666
Really? How about you have
a go at me, ya lumpy brute.

999
00:59:47,833 --> 00:59:48,918
- Bring it on!
- Come on!

1000
00:59:49,001 --> 00:59:50,044
L3!

1001
00:59:50,127 --> 00:59:52,088
Droid rights!
We are sentient!

1002
00:59:52,254 --> 00:59:54,256
I'm gonna flip your switch.

1003
00:59:54,965 --> 00:59:56,342
Good luck finding it.

1004
00:59:56,509 --> 00:59:57,927
L3!

1005
00:59:59,345 --> 01:00:01,138
Let go of the mean man's face.

1006
01:00:01,305 --> 01:00:02,306
We're leaving.

1007
01:00:02,473 --> 01:00:04,391
They don't even
serve our kind here.

1008
01:00:04,558 --> 01:00:05,601
Now.

1009
01:00:09,313 --> 01:00:10,648
Who are these guys?

1010
01:00:10,815 --> 01:00:12,274
We're taking them to Kessel.

1011
01:00:12,817 --> 01:00:14,235
Are we?

1012
01:00:14,401 --> 01:00:16,487
And what if I don't elect
to go to Kessel?

1013
01:00:16,987 --> 01:00:18,155
Please don't start.

1014
01:00:18,322 --> 01:00:19,532
Or what, you'll have me wiped?

1015
01:00:19,698 --> 01:00:22,076
You couldn't get from here to
Black Spire without me.

1016
01:00:22,243 --> 01:00:23,786
Now you're gonna
make the Kessel Run?

1017
01:00:23,953 --> 01:00:25,871
If she doesn't wanna fly,
I'll be your co-pilot.

1018
01:00:26,038 --> 01:00:27,665
- I don't mind.
- No, no. It's okay.

1019
01:00:27,832 --> 01:00:29,083
She's definitely going.

1020
01:00:29,250 --> 01:00:32,169
Why? Because
you're my organic overlord?

1021
01:00:32,336 --> 01:00:34,380
Because I'm your
captain, how about that?

1022
01:00:34,547 --> 01:00:36,757
I actually would have
her memory wiped,

1023
01:00:36,924 --> 01:00:38,175
but she's got the best damn

1024
01:00:38,259 --> 01:00:39,927
navigational database
in the galaxy.

1025
01:00:40,427 --> 01:00:42,012
Could use a fresh coat
of paint, though!

1026
01:00:42,179 --> 01:00:45,474
Landonis, you do not want to
press that button with me.

1027
01:00:46,642 --> 01:00:49,270
You know, a lot of
ships around here get boosted.

1028
01:00:49,436 --> 01:00:51,480
So, I keep mine locked up.

1029
01:00:51,647 --> 01:00:53,357
You know, for safety.

1030
01:00:54,108 --> 01:00:56,318
L3, do you mind?

1031
01:01:02,324 --> 01:01:03,784
Look away.

1032
01:01:03,951 --> 01:01:05,202
I can't perform
with you looking at me.

1033
01:01:05,661 --> 01:01:06,662
Please indulge her.

1034
01:01:14,962 --> 01:01:17,214
I can feel you looking at me.

1035
01:01:21,927 --> 01:01:23,596
What are we doing here?

1036
01:01:23,762 --> 01:01:24,805
This guy's a hustler.

1037
01:01:24,889 --> 01:01:26,223
I don't even think
he's got a ship.

1038
01:01:26,390 --> 01:01:27,975
If he does, it's gonna be
a piece of junk

1039
01:01:28,058 --> 01:01:29,059
if it's even here.

1040
01:01:29,226 --> 01:01:32,021
There she is, my pride and joy.

1041
01:01:32,938 --> 01:01:34,190
The Millennium Falcon.

1042
01:01:49,580 --> 01:01:51,707
Looks like you had
a little work done.

1043
01:01:51,874 --> 01:01:53,375
Indeed I have, Han.

1044
01:01:53,542 --> 01:01:56,003
Installed an escape pod
in the mandible notch,

1045
01:01:56,170 --> 01:01:58,589
alluvial dampers, a wet bar.

1046
01:01:58,756 --> 01:02:00,591
And a fortified infraction

1047
01:02:00,674 --> 01:02:02,801
restraint on the landing gear.

1048
01:02:02,968 --> 01:02:05,930
Looks to me like they
impounded your ship, Lando.

1049
01:02:06,764 --> 01:02:08,349
This is unbelievable!

1050
01:02:08,515 --> 01:02:09,892
I'm definitely
gonna have some words

1051
01:02:09,975 --> 01:02:12,019
with someone about this.

1052
01:02:13,604 --> 01:02:15,272
You must have experience
with these, right?

1053
01:02:15,689 --> 01:02:17,274
Yeah, I could take it off.

1054
01:02:17,441 --> 01:02:18,567
Fantastic!

1055
01:02:18,734 --> 01:02:20,569
Along with five percent
off your cut.

1056
01:02:21,237 --> 01:02:23,072
You're down to 20.

1057
01:02:25,741 --> 01:02:27,493
I don't like it.

1058
01:02:27,660 --> 01:02:29,286
I don't agree with it.

1059
01:02:30,287 --> 01:02:31,497
But I accept it.

1060
01:02:32,831 --> 01:02:34,708
You're getting
the hang of this, Lando.

1061
01:02:35,292 --> 01:02:36,502
Yeah.

1062
01:02:36,835 --> 01:02:37,878
Come on, Chewie.

1063
01:02:38,045 --> 01:02:39,046
Gonna need a little bit of

1064
01:02:39,129 --> 01:02:40,547
that Wookiee oomph.

1065
01:02:42,341 --> 01:02:43,842
Yourplan is underway, Enfys.

1066
01:02:43,926 --> 01:02:45,886
We've attached
the homing beacon.

1067
01:02:46,053 --> 01:02:47,221
They won't elude us now.

1068
01:02:47,304 --> 01:02:48,305
Good.

1069
01:02:53,769 --> 01:02:57,231
If they survive,
they'll bring the prize to us.

1070
01:03:12,579 --> 01:03:14,957
This is a Corellian YT-1300.

1071
01:03:15,541 --> 01:03:17,918
You know your stuff.

1072
01:03:18,085 --> 01:03:19,670
I've been on one before.

1073
01:03:19,837 --> 01:03:21,171
My dad worked the line

1074
01:03:21,255 --> 01:03:23,966
at the CEC plant
before he got laid off.

1075
01:03:24,425 --> 01:03:25,801
He built these.

1076
01:03:26,969 --> 01:03:29,346
He wanted to be a pilot, but...

1077
01:03:29,513 --> 01:03:31,724
You close with your old man?

1078
01:03:32,474 --> 01:03:33,517
Not really.

1079
01:03:33,684 --> 01:03:35,811
Yeah, me neither.

1080
01:03:35,978 --> 01:03:37,938
My mom, on the other hand,

1081
01:03:38,105 --> 01:03:40,107
most amazing woman
I've ever known.

1082
01:03:43,485 --> 01:03:44,570
Excuse me.

1083
01:03:44,737 --> 01:03:47,448
Get your presumptuous ass
out of my seat!

1084
01:03:53,120 --> 01:03:55,956
My sacral-occipital
circuit is sticking.

1085
01:03:56,123 --> 01:03:57,708
You're gonna have
to do that thing again later.

1086
01:03:58,417 --> 01:03:59,668
Yeah.

1087
01:04:00,085 --> 01:04:02,087
All right,
course to Kessel is set.

1088
01:04:02,254 --> 01:04:03,839
Plugging coordinates in now.

1089
01:04:04,006 --> 01:04:05,257
Just keep your pinky on the yoke

1090
01:04:05,424 --> 01:04:06,633
and try not to mess anything up.

1091
01:04:06,800 --> 01:04:07,801
Whatever you say, my lady.

1092
01:04:07,885 --> 01:04:09,470
Just let me know when
you're ready to jump.

1093
01:04:09,636 --> 01:04:11,347
Ready in...

1094
01:04:13,390 --> 01:04:14,391
Ready.

1095
01:04:15,684 --> 01:04:18,145
It's just a simple jump to
hyperspace, and we're there.

1096
01:04:18,312 --> 01:04:19,438
What's so tricky about that?

1097
01:04:19,605 --> 01:04:21,732
Plenty. Can't plot
a direct course to Kessel.

1098
01:04:21,899 --> 01:04:23,692
You have to thread through
the Si'Klaata Cluster

1099
01:04:23,859 --> 01:04:25,778
and then pass through
The Maelstrom.

1100
01:04:26,362 --> 01:04:28,238
You done flirting?
I'm still ready.

1101
01:04:29,406 --> 01:04:31,283
You might wanna buckle up, baby.

1102
01:04:51,845 --> 01:04:52,930
Think.

1103
01:04:53,097 --> 01:04:54,681
Do you wanna make that move?

1104
01:04:54,848 --> 01:04:56,809
Do you wanna make that move?

1105
01:04:57,226 --> 01:04:59,103
You made that move, okay.

1106
01:04:59,269 --> 01:05:01,897
I guess I have to
destroy that little guy.

1107
01:05:02,064 --> 01:05:04,316
Somehow I never
get bored with winning.

1108
01:05:05,651 --> 01:05:08,320
No, you can't wipe 'em off.
They're holograms.

1109
01:05:09,571 --> 01:05:11,365
Hey, hey, hey!
Chewie, relax!

1110
01:05:11,532 --> 01:05:13,659
Hey, try to compose yourself.

1111
01:05:13,826 --> 01:05:15,744
Look. All you gotta do is
think a few moves ahead,

1112
01:05:15,911 --> 01:05:17,079
anticipate your opponent.

1113
01:05:17,246 --> 01:05:19,790
There's a lesson
to be learned here.

1114
01:05:19,957 --> 01:05:20,999
You guys seen Qi'ra?

1115
01:05:23,627 --> 01:05:25,462
People are predictable.

1116
01:05:47,276 --> 01:05:49,361
Yeah, I had to try one on.

1117
01:05:49,778 --> 01:05:50,988
That's a lot of capes.

1118
01:05:51,155 --> 01:05:52,948
Maybe too many capes.

1119
01:05:57,578 --> 01:05:58,829
So what's the plan?

1120
01:05:59,246 --> 01:06:00,497
Well, I thought
we'd talk a little first

1121
01:06:00,581 --> 01:06:01,582
and then you know...

1122
01:06:02,624 --> 01:06:04,293
For Kessel.

1123
01:06:04,668 --> 01:06:06,128
Good.

1124
01:06:06,295 --> 01:06:08,005
Yeah? How good?

1125
01:06:08,172 --> 01:06:09,173
Foolproof.

1126
01:06:09,339 --> 01:06:10,841
Well, it better be.

1127
01:06:10,924 --> 01:06:11,925
- I...
- I...

1128
01:06:12,009 --> 01:06:13,093
- You go first.
- No.

1129
01:06:13,260 --> 01:06:14,595
What were you gonna say?

1130
01:06:14,928 --> 01:06:17,681
I wanna tell you so much.

1131
01:06:18,432 --> 01:06:19,892
And I wanna know everything

1132
01:06:19,975 --> 01:06:21,810
that's happened to you
since Corellia.

1133
01:06:23,103 --> 01:06:25,522
I'm not sure
we have that kinda time.

1134
01:06:25,689 --> 01:06:26,815
We could.

1135
01:06:26,982 --> 01:06:29,234
We could have all the time
we want after the job.

1136
01:06:29,401 --> 01:06:30,903
You and I.

1137
01:06:31,069 --> 01:06:32,070
What?

1138
01:06:33,155 --> 01:06:34,490
I want to.

1139
01:06:35,199 --> 01:06:36,408
You want to?

1140
01:06:36,575 --> 01:06:38,869
To tell you everything
that's happened.

1141
01:06:40,370 --> 01:06:42,498
But I know if I do,
you won't look at me the same.

1142
01:06:42,873 --> 01:06:44,625
The way that you're
looking at me right now.

1143
01:06:44,708 --> 01:06:45,751
Nothing is gonna change the way

1144
01:06:45,834 --> 01:06:46,835
I'm looking at you right now.

1145
01:06:46,919 --> 01:06:49,129
You don't know that.
You don't know what I've done.

1146
01:07:03,185 --> 01:07:04,728
Am I interrupting something?

1147
01:07:07,105 --> 01:07:08,106
Kinda.

1148
01:07:08,899 --> 01:07:09,900
Good.

1149
01:07:10,067 --> 01:07:11,735
'Cause we got
a lot of work to do.

1150
01:07:12,402 --> 01:07:13,779
You're making a big mistake.

1151
01:07:13,946 --> 01:07:14,947
- Really?
- Which is yours to make

1152
01:07:15,113 --> 01:07:17,241
except when you start to
interfere with my livelihood.

1153
01:07:17,324 --> 01:07:18,325
This isn't gonna interfere
with your livelihood.

1154
01:07:18,408 --> 01:07:19,409
Then we have a problem.

1155
01:07:19,493 --> 01:07:21,912
You don't see it,
because you don't want to.

1156
01:07:22,079 --> 01:07:23,705
Maybe I know her
a little better than you do.

1157
01:07:23,872 --> 01:07:26,333
Maybe you don't know
her well enough.

1158
01:07:27,042 --> 01:07:28,085
All right?

1159
01:07:28,168 --> 01:07:29,586
Look.

1160
01:07:30,087 --> 01:07:31,547
I like you, kid.

1161
01:07:31,713 --> 01:07:34,258
We got a good thing going
here. Me, you, Chewie.

1162
01:07:34,341 --> 01:07:35,342
- Yeah.
- Right?

1163
01:07:35,425 --> 01:07:37,177
The makings of a solid crew.

1164
01:07:37,344 --> 01:07:39,346
But it does not work with Qi'ra.

1165
01:07:39,888 --> 01:07:42,140
It worked with Val.
You trusted her.

1166
01:07:44,101 --> 01:07:46,979
You wanna know how I've
survived as long as I have?

1167
01:07:47,646 --> 01:07:49,022
I trust no one.

1168
01:07:50,482 --> 01:07:52,943
Assume everyone will betray you

1169
01:07:53,026 --> 01:07:54,945
and you will never
be disappointed.

1170
01:07:56,238 --> 01:07:58,407
Sounds like
a lonely way to live.

1171
01:07:59,032 --> 01:08:01,076
It's the only way.

1172
01:08:08,000 --> 01:08:09,126
Dropping out of lightspeed now.

1173
01:08:09,293 --> 01:08:10,335
Ready to...

1174
01:08:15,924 --> 01:08:18,093
The Akkadese Maelstrom.

1175
01:08:19,886 --> 01:08:21,263
I'm gonna go check
on the dampers.

1176
01:08:21,346 --> 01:08:22,347
You need anything?

1177
01:08:22,514 --> 01:08:24,057
Equal rights?

1178
01:08:54,212 --> 01:08:55,339
What's that sound?

1179
01:08:55,505 --> 01:08:58,759
Carbonbergs, size of planets,
crashing into each other.

1180
01:08:58,925 --> 01:09:00,886
Ships fly in there,
they never come out.

1181
01:09:01,053 --> 01:09:02,929
It's ionized gas, water vapor,

1182
01:09:03,096 --> 01:09:04,848
possibly vacuum-breathing
life forms

1183
01:09:04,931 --> 01:09:06,224
swirling around The Maw.

1184
01:09:06,391 --> 01:09:07,976
Only way in or out
is this channel.

1185
01:09:09,978 --> 01:09:12,230
So what are you gonna do
about your little problem?

1186
01:09:12,606 --> 01:09:13,732
Problem?

1187
01:09:15,651 --> 01:09:16,777
Well, that brand on your wrist

1188
01:09:16,860 --> 01:09:18,070
tells me that you're committed.

1189
01:09:18,654 --> 01:09:20,697
And that young male's
heart fluctuations

1190
01:09:20,781 --> 01:09:22,032
tell me he's in love with you.

1191
01:09:22,199 --> 01:09:24,493
Han is not in love with me!

1192
01:09:26,036 --> 01:09:27,913
Please. It's just us.

1193
01:09:28,080 --> 01:09:31,333
You don't have to pretend.
I'm in the same situation.

1194
01:09:31,416 --> 01:09:32,417
You are?

1195
01:09:32,501 --> 01:09:33,543
I'm sure you've noticed

1196
01:09:33,710 --> 01:09:34,920
that Lando has feelings for me.

1197
01:09:35,003 --> 01:09:36,546
Which makes
working together difficult

1198
01:09:36,713 --> 01:09:38,882
because I do not feel
the same way about him.

1199
01:09:39,049 --> 01:09:40,300
Right.

1200
01:09:40,467 --> 01:09:41,968
Yes, yeah.

1201
01:09:42,135 --> 01:09:43,553
Yeah, I see that.

1202
01:09:43,720 --> 01:09:46,515
Sometimes, I think... Maybe.

1203
01:09:47,307 --> 01:09:48,642
But, no.

1204
01:09:50,477 --> 01:09:52,270
We're just not compatible.

1205
01:09:54,189 --> 01:09:55,941
How would that work?

1206
01:09:56,441 --> 01:09:57,442
It works.

1207
01:10:07,953 --> 01:10:09,746
This is a precision job.

1208
01:10:09,913 --> 01:10:12,374
Thermal vault will be
on the lowest level.

1209
01:10:12,457 --> 01:10:13,834
Down where it's warm.

1210
01:10:14,000 --> 01:10:15,627
The only way
we're gonna pull this off

1211
01:10:15,794 --> 01:10:18,255
is if everybody
plays their part.

1212
01:10:18,422 --> 01:10:20,215
Stick to the plan.

1213
01:10:20,382 --> 01:10:22,718
Do not improvise.

1214
01:10:27,264 --> 01:10:29,433
Mining colonies are the worst.

1215
01:10:29,599 --> 01:10:31,435
Yeah, well, "the worst"

1216
01:10:31,518 --> 01:10:32,894
is where the money is.

1217
01:10:35,021 --> 01:10:37,149
All right, people.
Time to shine.

1218
01:11:13,685 --> 01:11:15,312
It won't be for long.

1219
01:11:15,479 --> 01:11:17,147
Shut up, the both of you.

1220
01:11:17,439 --> 01:11:19,524
I am Oksana Floren,

1221
01:11:19,691 --> 01:11:21,693
Deputy Assistant Administrator
to the Vice-Admiral

1222
01:11:21,860 --> 01:11:24,571
of the Federation of
Trade Route Allocation

1223
01:11:24,654 --> 01:11:25,906
and Monetization.

1224
01:11:26,114 --> 01:11:29,201
Here with an offer
from his eminence,

1225
01:11:29,284 --> 01:11:30,744
the Senior Vice-Admiral.

1226
01:11:31,328 --> 01:11:34,206
Your spice for our
hard-working slaves.

1227
01:11:34,372 --> 01:11:35,707
I brought you a sample.

1228
01:11:35,874 --> 01:11:38,543
Tuul, bring forth
the merchandise.

1229
01:12:07,280 --> 01:12:08,949
Director Tolsite said our slaves

1230
01:12:09,032 --> 01:12:10,116
should follow those guys

1231
01:12:10,283 --> 01:12:11,952
to get clipped and tagged.

1232
01:12:12,118 --> 01:12:13,662
What are they clipping?

1233
01:12:18,124 --> 01:12:19,125
He wants us to follow him.

1234
01:12:23,463 --> 01:12:24,464
Really?

1235
01:12:24,631 --> 01:12:25,882
That's for that stunt
you pulled earlier,

1236
01:12:25,966 --> 01:12:27,133
you degenerate scum.

1237
01:12:46,486 --> 01:12:48,446
He says all systems
in this sector

1238
01:12:48,530 --> 01:12:50,240
of the facility operate
out of this room.

1239
01:12:50,407 --> 01:12:52,325
It's how they're able
to maintain control

1240
01:12:52,409 --> 01:12:54,077
over so many with so few.

1241
01:12:58,206 --> 01:13:00,250
The director says
their reconditioning process

1242
01:13:00,333 --> 01:13:02,544
is excruciating but effective.

1243
01:13:17,809 --> 01:13:20,061
He said your security attaché
can wait there.

1244
01:13:20,228 --> 01:13:22,480
"Surely, we don't need him
to negotiate."

1245
01:13:25,108 --> 01:13:26,401
Wait there, Tuul.

1246
01:13:26,568 --> 01:13:28,486
Try not to bother anyone.

1247
01:13:53,219 --> 01:13:54,471
Nice!

1248
01:13:54,971 --> 01:13:56,014
That was the uniform

1249
01:13:56,097 --> 01:13:58,391
that would've fit me
perfectly, but it's fine.

1250
01:14:04,022 --> 01:14:05,065
What is it?

1251
01:14:08,109 --> 01:14:09,903
Would you mind
holding this for me?

1252
01:14:25,460 --> 01:14:27,128
I have never see anyone do...

1253
01:14:27,295 --> 01:14:28,380
What was that?

1254
01:14:28,713 --> 01:14:30,757
Teräs Käsi.

1255
01:14:32,008 --> 01:14:33,009
Dryden taught me.

1256
01:14:39,432 --> 01:14:40,517
Well negotiated.

1257
01:14:50,819 --> 01:14:52,654
Excuse me.
I need to use this terminal.

1258
01:14:52,737 --> 01:14:53,738
Hello?

1259
01:14:55,115 --> 01:14:56,866
Can you hear me?

1260
01:14:58,118 --> 01:14:59,536
Restraining bolts...

1261
01:14:59,869 --> 01:15:00,912
Barbaric.

1262
01:15:03,123 --> 01:15:05,125
Congratulations!
You're liberated. Scoot.

1263
01:15:05,208 --> 01:15:06,209
I don't know.

1264
01:15:06,292 --> 01:15:07,293
Free your brothers and sisters
or something.

1265
01:15:07,460 --> 01:15:09,421
Just give me some space.

1266
01:15:15,176 --> 01:15:16,386
I'm in!

1267
01:15:16,553 --> 01:15:17,637
Han, can you hear me?

1268
01:15:17,804 --> 01:15:18,930
I kinda need to
know which way to go here.

1269
01:15:19,180 --> 01:15:20,181
L3?

1270
01:15:20,348 --> 01:15:22,058
The thermal vault
is down two levels,

1271
01:15:22,225 --> 01:15:23,727
then left, then right,
then it's the third left.

1272
01:15:23,893 --> 01:15:27,105
Right. That's a lot of
directions, but we're on it.

1273
01:15:34,154 --> 01:15:35,321
They're in subsector four,

1274
01:15:35,488 --> 01:15:37,782
coming up on gate X-3-7-1 -K.

1275
01:15:37,949 --> 01:15:39,159
Overriding!

1276
01:15:45,498 --> 01:15:46,624
Freedom.

1277
01:16:08,772 --> 01:16:10,899
What the hell are you
guys doing up there?

1278
01:16:11,066 --> 01:16:12,984
I created a distraction!

1279
01:16:18,031 --> 01:16:19,032
Come on! This way!

1280
01:16:22,118 --> 01:16:23,787
Wait! What are you doing?

1281
01:16:24,245 --> 01:16:25,789
Come on,
we gotta get the coaxium.

1282
01:16:27,874 --> 01:16:30,168
Hey! Remember what Beckett
said, stick to the plan.

1283
01:16:30,376 --> 01:16:33,338
Chewie! Come on, let's go!

1284
01:16:36,508 --> 01:16:37,509
Fine!

1285
01:16:39,719 --> 01:16:40,804
Chewie!

1286
01:16:43,556 --> 01:16:44,974
Here, you might need this.

1287
01:16:50,230 --> 01:16:52,232
Hope I see you around sometime.

1288
01:17:08,123 --> 01:17:09,290
Han, where are you?

1289
01:17:09,457 --> 01:17:10,917
I'm on my way to the vault.

1290
01:17:11,084 --> 01:17:12,335
I lost Chewie.

1291
01:17:12,418 --> 01:17:13,419
He's dead?

1292
01:17:13,586 --> 01:17:15,046
No, he had something
he had to do.

1293
01:17:15,213 --> 01:17:16,339
Is he coming back?

1294
01:17:16,506 --> 01:17:17,549
I don't know.

1295
01:17:18,925 --> 01:17:20,802
Okay, they're on to us now.

1296
01:17:30,603 --> 01:17:31,604
I'm at the vault.

1297
01:17:39,571 --> 01:17:41,114
That's what I said!

1298
01:17:44,534 --> 01:17:46,369
- That was impressive.
- Yeah.

1299
01:17:46,744 --> 01:17:47,829
We're clear.

1300
01:17:58,381 --> 01:17:59,507
Now what?

1301
01:17:59,674 --> 01:18:01,467
Han, each canister
should be equipped

1302
01:18:01,551 --> 01:18:02,594
with a thermal display.

1303
01:18:02,760 --> 01:18:03,928
Yeah, I see it.

1304
01:18:04,095 --> 01:18:06,806
If the internal temperature
reaches below 35 standard,

1305
01:18:06,973 --> 01:18:09,976
then the coaxium
will destabilize and explode.

1306
01:18:10,143 --> 01:18:12,478
Yup, I get it, guys.
It's dangerous.

1307
01:18:21,487 --> 01:18:22,739
Okay, got it.

1308
01:18:23,114 --> 01:18:24,866
Great. Only eleven more.

1309
01:18:25,200 --> 01:18:26,201
Eleven?

1310
01:18:33,833 --> 01:18:36,794
The Calrissian Chronicles,
chapter five.

1311
01:18:37,003 --> 01:18:38,296
Continued.

1312
01:18:38,463 --> 01:18:40,423
Personally, I wasn't all that
impressed with the Sharu.

1313
01:18:40,590 --> 01:18:42,842
No sense of humor or style.

1314
01:18:43,009 --> 01:18:44,928
Nonetheless, there L3 and I were

1315
01:18:45,094 --> 01:18:46,804
deep in their sacred temple.

1316
01:18:46,971 --> 01:18:48,723
And that's when we saw it...

1317
01:18:51,351 --> 01:18:52,894
Always something.

1318
01:18:55,313 --> 01:18:57,023
You guys are not gonna believe
what I'm seeing up here.

1319
01:18:57,190 --> 01:18:59,067
Is it a mass breakout?

1320
01:18:59,692 --> 01:19:00,735
L3, what did you do?

1321
01:19:00,902 --> 01:19:02,737
I found my true purpose, Lando.

1322
01:19:02,904 --> 01:19:04,030
That's what I've done.

1323
01:19:05,907 --> 01:19:08,117
I'm so glad we took this job!

1324
01:19:08,326 --> 01:19:09,702
That droid!

1325
01:19:09,786 --> 01:19:10,787
L3, come on!

1326
01:19:13,831 --> 01:19:15,416
Follow me, compatriots!

1327
01:19:22,924 --> 01:19:24,509
Another couple guards
just spotted me.

1328
01:19:24,676 --> 01:19:26,594
I don't have a free hand
to take 'em out.

1329
01:19:26,761 --> 01:19:28,179
- What do I do?
- Improvise.

1330
01:19:28,388 --> 01:19:30,306
You said never improvise!

1331
01:19:38,982 --> 01:19:40,400
Hi!

1332
01:19:40,566 --> 01:19:41,609
Don't forget that guy!

1333
01:19:57,959 --> 01:19:59,544
Good to see you, buddy!

1334
01:20:00,295 --> 01:20:02,213
Stay with me, Sagwa!
Keep up!

1335
01:20:05,591 --> 01:20:06,968
Hey! I'm Chewie's friend, Han.

1336
01:20:09,721 --> 01:20:11,014
Okay.

1337
01:20:29,824 --> 01:20:30,950
They're stealing the coaxium.

1338
01:20:31,117 --> 01:20:32,118
Disable that freighter!

1339
01:20:38,207 --> 01:20:40,084
Han!

1340
01:20:42,170 --> 01:20:43,171
Hey!

1341
01:20:54,140 --> 01:20:55,141
Follow me.

1342
01:20:57,894 --> 01:20:59,437
Rebellion!

1343
01:21:10,239 --> 01:21:11,866
They're going for
the landing gear!

1344
01:21:11,949 --> 01:21:13,117
We've gotta get out of here!

1345
01:21:15,203 --> 01:21:17,246
We need to keep 'em away
from those cannons!

1346
01:21:25,463 --> 01:21:26,672
Catch that!

1347
01:21:29,258 --> 01:21:31,344
Coaxium's stowed!
Let's go!

1348
01:21:31,511 --> 01:21:32,929
Where's L3?

1349
01:21:33,096 --> 01:21:35,723
No more subjugation!

1350
01:21:40,395 --> 01:21:41,396
L3!

1351
01:21:41,562 --> 01:21:43,564
No, Lando!
Get back here!

1352
01:21:46,275 --> 01:21:47,568
Lando!

1353
01:21:48,319 --> 01:21:50,530
System failure.

1354
01:21:50,696 --> 01:21:52,448
Have to reroute
the sensory modulators.

1355
01:21:52,615 --> 01:21:54,325
It's all right.
Save your energy.

1356
01:21:54,492 --> 01:21:55,952
I'm gonna get you outta here.
All right?

1357
01:21:56,119 --> 01:21:57,954
System failure...

1358
01:22:03,084 --> 01:22:04,085
Rerouting...

1359
01:22:05,753 --> 01:22:06,796
Damn it!

1360
01:22:06,879 --> 01:22:07,880
Han!

1361
01:22:14,095 --> 01:22:15,096
Sagwa.

1362
01:22:15,263 --> 01:22:16,681
This way!

1363
01:22:17,140 --> 01:22:18,349
Come, come!

1364
01:22:28,818 --> 01:22:30,486
Chewie!
Damn it!

1365
01:22:34,198 --> 01:22:35,741
It's not responding.

1366
01:22:53,426 --> 01:22:55,428
What are you
standing around for? Come on!

1367
01:23:00,892 --> 01:23:02,435
It's okay, you'll be fine.

1368
01:23:03,728 --> 01:23:05,771
It's not responding...
Not responding...

1369
01:23:06,522 --> 01:23:07,732
Han, get us out of here.

1370
01:23:08,566 --> 01:23:09,567
It's not responding.

1371
01:23:09,734 --> 01:23:11,277
Han! Now!

1372
01:23:11,486 --> 01:23:12,487
On it.

1373
01:23:40,681 --> 01:23:42,350
- Lando...
- I'm here.

1374
01:23:42,642 --> 01:23:44,101
- It's all right, L3.
- Lando...

1375
01:23:44,268 --> 01:23:45,353
- I've got you.
- This is not...

1376
01:23:45,561 --> 01:23:46,812
- It's okay, L3.
- Lando.

1377
01:23:47,271 --> 01:23:49,273
It's all right. I can fix you.
I can fix you.

1378
01:23:49,732 --> 01:23:50,983
Lando.

1379
01:23:51,150 --> 01:23:53,152
What's happening to me?

1380
01:23:55,571 --> 01:23:56,989
L3?

1381
01:23:57,615 --> 01:23:58,908
L3!

1382
01:24:05,748 --> 01:24:07,875
I'm sorry, girl.

1383
01:24:08,042 --> 01:24:10,044
I'm so sorry.

1384
01:24:23,516 --> 01:24:24,809
I could use a co-pilot.

1385
01:24:49,250 --> 01:24:50,668
Sorry.

1386
01:24:53,546 --> 01:24:54,547
With the cargo we're carrying,

1387
01:24:54,630 --> 01:24:55,715
if we don't make up
some lost time

1388
01:24:55,881 --> 01:24:57,925
we're gonna be in real trouble.

1389
01:24:58,092 --> 01:24:59,594
How about that?
Is that real trouble?

1390
01:25:06,267 --> 01:25:08,519
That is an Imperial blockade.

1391
01:25:08,686 --> 01:25:10,563
What's it doing here?

1392
01:25:10,730 --> 01:25:12,607
Probably heard about
your little rebellion.

1393
01:25:13,816 --> 01:25:15,860
Nope.
Not gonna make it.

1394
01:25:16,027 --> 01:25:17,069
We're gonna have to
drop the shipment.

1395
01:25:17,236 --> 01:25:19,655
If we don't deliver,
Dryden will kill us.

1396
01:25:19,822 --> 01:25:21,282
All right, trust me,
I know these guys.

1397
01:25:21,365 --> 01:25:22,491
I used to be one of 'em.

1398
01:25:22,658 --> 01:25:24,452
There's no way they're
gonna waste a TIE fighter

1399
01:25:24,619 --> 01:25:26,621
chasing down a little
rinky-dink freighter.

1400
01:25:31,042 --> 01:25:32,043
You were saying?

1401
01:25:32,209 --> 01:25:33,586
Usually, in situations like this

1402
01:25:33,753 --> 01:25:35,838
I like to turn around
in the opposite direction.

1403
01:25:45,014 --> 01:25:46,515
I'm on the ventral gun.

1404
01:25:51,687 --> 01:25:52,688
It's an easy equation.

1405
01:25:52,855 --> 01:25:55,024
We simply don't have enough
time to get to Savareen

1406
01:25:55,107 --> 01:25:56,108
before the canisters explode!

1407
01:25:56,275 --> 01:25:57,526
Just have to find
a faster route.

1408
01:25:57,693 --> 01:25:58,903
There isn't one!
You can't make

1409
01:25:58,986 --> 01:26:00,529
the Kessel Run in less than
20 parsecs.

1410
01:26:00,613 --> 01:26:01,947
- Watch me.
- How?

1411
01:26:02,114 --> 01:26:03,407
Take a shortcut, through there.

1412
01:26:04,992 --> 01:26:06,243
Into The Maelstrom?

1413
01:26:07,161 --> 01:26:08,913
Spectacular way of killing
us all, I'll give you that.

1414
01:26:09,080 --> 01:26:10,706
- Can't do it without L3.
- She's gone!

1415
01:26:10,873 --> 01:26:12,208
You said yourself
she's got the best

1416
01:26:12,291 --> 01:26:13,751
navigational database
in the galaxy.

1417
01:26:13,918 --> 01:26:15,503
If we remove her neural core,

1418
01:26:15,670 --> 01:26:16,879
it's possible we can
download her brain

1419
01:26:16,962 --> 01:26:18,422
into the Falcon's
navicomputer, right?

1420
01:26:18,506 --> 01:26:19,507
Could we?

1421
01:26:19,924 --> 01:26:20,925
Theoretically.

1422
01:26:21,092 --> 01:26:22,968
Only one way to find out.

1423
01:26:25,805 --> 01:26:28,182
I got a really good feeling
about this.

1424
01:26:42,196 --> 01:26:43,739
Oops, that's on me.

1425
01:26:50,496 --> 01:26:51,831
Okay.

1426
01:26:54,208 --> 01:26:56,001
Beckett, you see them?
They still on us?

1427
01:26:59,171 --> 01:27:00,464
Beckett, did you hear me?

1428
01:27:00,548 --> 01:27:01,966
Are they on us?

1429
01:27:02,133 --> 01:27:03,759
Like rashnold on a kalak.

1430
01:27:04,719 --> 01:27:06,178
I don't know what that means.

1431
01:27:06,345 --> 01:27:08,139
Like a gingleson's pelt.

1432
01:27:08,806 --> 01:27:10,266
What? Are they or aren't they?

1433
01:27:10,433 --> 01:27:11,809
Yes, they're still on us!

1434
01:27:19,150 --> 01:27:23,654
This is why you never let
anyone fly your ship.

1435
01:27:23,821 --> 01:27:25,072
Come on!

1436
01:27:29,368 --> 01:27:31,912
Yeah, one just got past me.
He's right on top of us!

1437
01:27:41,422 --> 01:27:43,174
Good going, Han!

1438
01:27:48,846 --> 01:27:50,222
We need to
divert auxiliary power

1439
01:27:50,306 --> 01:27:51,307
to the rear deflector shield.

1440
01:27:51,474 --> 01:27:53,809
We definitely do!

1441
01:28:01,025 --> 01:28:02,526
Since when do you know
how to fly?

1442
01:28:05,196 --> 01:28:06,947
190 years old?

1443
01:28:08,866 --> 01:28:10,117
You look great!

1444
01:28:11,160 --> 01:28:12,203
Chewie, get in.

1445
01:28:12,369 --> 01:28:13,412
I'll help Lando.

1446
01:28:28,552 --> 01:28:31,055
That's my cape!

1447
01:28:31,222 --> 01:28:32,348
That's a custom piece!

1448
01:28:40,105 --> 01:28:41,899
What? Beckett, you with us?

1449
01:28:42,066 --> 01:28:43,859
We just lost the cannon!

1450
01:28:44,485 --> 01:28:46,320
And I really hurt my thumbs.

1451
01:28:46,487 --> 01:28:48,113
There's still one on us.

1452
01:28:53,661 --> 01:28:55,079
Drop the landing gear.

1453
01:28:55,955 --> 01:28:57,623
When I tell you,
flood the intake

1454
01:28:57,706 --> 01:28:58,916
and sweep to the bi-lats.

1455
01:29:02,378 --> 01:29:05,256
A little something I picked up
from my pal, Needles,

1456
01:29:05,422 --> 01:29:07,424
best street racer
in all of Corellia.

1457
01:29:08,259 --> 01:29:09,552
Till he crashed

1458
01:29:09,718 --> 01:29:11,554
and died, doing this.

1459
01:29:29,864 --> 01:29:31,490
Flood it, it's all yours!

1460
01:29:43,377 --> 01:29:45,713
Nice move!

1461
01:29:48,632 --> 01:29:50,509
Pull out her internal processor.

1462
01:29:53,304 --> 01:29:54,430
Sorry.

1463
01:30:00,603 --> 01:30:01,604
We've got L3.

1464
01:30:04,106 --> 01:30:05,441
Remove the mod calibrator.

1465
01:30:05,524 --> 01:30:06,567
Make sure
the T-Line's connected.

1466
01:30:06,650 --> 01:30:08,068
I'm gonna tuck it in.
Don't worry.

1467
01:30:08,152 --> 01:30:09,153
You close?

1468
01:30:09,236 --> 01:30:11,614
That coaxium's
getting real ripe.

1469
01:30:12,031 --> 01:30:13,699
Okay.

1470
01:30:15,993 --> 01:30:17,661
She's interfacing.

1471
01:30:21,832 --> 01:30:23,918
She's part of the ship now.

1472
01:30:35,179 --> 01:30:36,388
Where the hell are we?

1473
01:30:36,555 --> 01:30:38,140
We're way off
the edge of the map.

1474
01:30:38,766 --> 01:30:39,767
Wait.

1475
01:30:39,934 --> 01:30:42,770
L3's constructing a model
of The Maelstrom.

1476
01:30:45,064 --> 01:30:47,316
She says we're
approaching The Maw.

1477
01:30:47,524 --> 01:30:48,817
That doesn't sound
like something

1478
01:30:48,901 --> 01:30:50,319
we wanna be approaching.

1479
01:31:11,340 --> 01:31:12,341
Hang on!

1480
01:31:17,638 --> 01:31:18,722
This is The Maw?

1481
01:31:18,889 --> 01:31:20,641
No, that's not The Maw.
I don't know what this is.

1482
01:31:20,808 --> 01:31:22,059
That's a living thing.

1483
01:31:36,407 --> 01:31:37,658
There!

1484
01:31:37,950 --> 01:31:39,076
That's The Maw.

1485
01:31:41,954 --> 01:31:43,455
It's a gravity well.

1486
01:31:43,622 --> 01:31:44,623
I got an idea.

1487
01:31:46,333 --> 01:31:47,918
Don't fly toward it, Han!

1488
01:31:55,634 --> 01:31:56,635
See if it goes for this.

1489
01:31:56,802 --> 01:31:58,637
No, what are you doing?
That's the escape pod!

1490
01:32:00,014 --> 01:32:01,181
I know.

1491
01:32:04,351 --> 01:32:05,436
Then why'd you do it?

1492
01:32:12,860 --> 01:32:14,236
That's why, baby.

1493
01:32:23,203 --> 01:32:24,204
She found a way out.

1494
01:32:25,080 --> 01:32:27,416
90 degrees,
to the left... ish.

1495
01:32:27,499 --> 01:32:28,500
Left-ish.

1496
01:32:28,667 --> 01:32:29,877
I can't.

1497
01:32:30,044 --> 01:32:31,670
It's taking everything we got
to stay out of The Maw.

1498
01:32:31,837 --> 01:32:33,672
It's pulling us in.
We're stuck.

1499
01:32:37,551 --> 01:32:39,803
We have enough raw coaxium
to power a dozen destroyers.

1500
01:32:39,970 --> 01:32:41,805
Inject it into the fuel line,
it'll blow up the ship.

1501
01:32:41,972 --> 01:32:42,973
Not the fuel line.

1502
01:32:43,849 --> 01:32:45,309
But if we put one drop
into the fusion reactor,

1503
01:32:45,392 --> 01:32:46,393
it might just...

1504
01:32:46,477 --> 01:32:47,561
Give us the kick we need.

1505
01:32:47,728 --> 01:32:49,688
All right, I'm on it!

1506
01:32:54,193 --> 01:32:55,778
I know, we're getting
dragged in a circle.

1507
01:33:09,917 --> 01:33:11,668
Once we get lined up,
it's gonna be a straight shot.

1508
01:33:11,835 --> 01:33:13,003
As soon as that coaxium ignites,

1509
01:33:13,087 --> 01:33:14,213
we're gonna tear out of here

1510
01:33:14,379 --> 01:33:15,672
and the second we're
clear of The Maelstrom,

1511
01:33:15,756 --> 01:33:17,091
we jump to lightspeed.

1512
01:33:21,011 --> 01:33:22,012
Beckett!

1513
01:33:22,346 --> 01:33:23,472
Can't talk!

1514
01:33:27,267 --> 01:33:28,310
I see it.

1515
01:33:52,960 --> 01:33:53,961
Beckett, hurry up!

1516
01:33:54,044 --> 01:33:56,004
We only get one shot
at this thing!

1517
01:33:56,380 --> 01:33:58,298
Shut up and let me do this!

1518
01:34:06,223 --> 01:34:08,809
Beckett, I'm gonna
count you down!

1519
01:34:10,018 --> 01:34:11,353
Three!

1520
01:34:14,148 --> 01:34:15,190
Two!

1521
01:34:19,528 --> 01:34:20,529
Now!

1522
01:34:20,612 --> 01:34:21,613
Now?

1523
01:34:21,697 --> 01:34:22,698
Now!

1524
01:34:39,047 --> 01:34:40,799
Shoot...

1525
01:34:53,645 --> 01:34:54,646
Chewie, when I tell you,
kick out the thrusters

1526
01:34:54,813 --> 01:34:56,648
- and jump to lightspeed.
- Wait, what are we...

1527
01:34:56,815 --> 01:34:57,816
Remember that alley
we slipped through

1528
01:34:57,900 --> 01:34:58,942
in the Santhe Shipyards?

1529
01:34:59,026 --> 01:35:00,736
Yeah, I remember!
I remember it didn't work.

1530
01:35:00,903 --> 01:35:01,987
This time it's gonna.

1531
01:35:12,414 --> 01:35:13,415
Punch it!

1532
01:35:24,509 --> 01:35:26,553
Savareen,
this is Millennium Falcon.

1533
01:35:26,720 --> 01:35:29,473
We have coaxium that needs
to be off-loaded immediately.

1534
01:35:29,640 --> 01:35:32,267
Like immediately, immediately!

1535
01:35:32,851 --> 01:35:34,269
We're here now...

1536
01:35:34,436 --> 01:35:35,520
...see you. I...

1537
01:36:06,635 --> 01:36:08,720
Just did the Kessel Run
in 12 parsecs.

1538
01:36:12,975 --> 01:36:14,476
Not if you round down, buddy.

1539
01:36:15,102 --> 01:36:16,103
Yeah.

1540
01:36:22,276 --> 01:36:24,736
She is a hell of a ship.

1541
01:36:33,120 --> 01:36:34,454
I hate you.

1542
01:36:34,621 --> 01:36:36,081
I know.

1543
01:36:38,625 --> 01:36:40,502
I'm gonna be on my ship,

1544
01:36:40,669 --> 01:36:42,337
in my quarters,

1545
01:36:42,504 --> 01:36:45,757
waiting for you
to bring me my share.

1546
01:36:47,843 --> 01:36:50,470
And then I don't ever
wanna see you again.

1547
01:36:54,808 --> 01:36:56,393
Never?

1548
01:37:10,032 --> 01:37:11,783
Where's your boss?

1549
01:37:12,242 --> 01:37:14,745
Don't worry.
He'll be here.

1550
01:37:15,704 --> 01:37:16,747
Then what?

1551
01:37:17,497 --> 01:37:20,167
Well, you delivered,

1552
01:37:20,334 --> 01:37:22,210
so you will get paid.

1553
01:37:22,377 --> 01:37:24,379
You can buy that ship.

1554
01:37:24,921 --> 01:37:28,258
You know that's not
what I'm asking.

1555
01:37:30,677 --> 01:37:32,304
It can't happen.

1556
01:37:36,683 --> 01:37:38,101
Because you're with Dryden?

1557
01:37:38,268 --> 01:37:41,355
I'm not with him, but I owe him.

1558
01:37:42,898 --> 01:37:45,108
He helped me out
of a bad situation.

1559
01:37:46,234 --> 01:37:48,278
And how long do you have
to pay off that debt?

1560
01:37:51,740 --> 01:37:54,117
Everyone serves somebody, Han.

1561
01:37:55,202 --> 01:37:57,204
Even Dryden Vos.

1562
01:37:57,496 --> 01:38:00,415
Look, you don't want to make
an enemy of Crimson Dawn

1563
01:38:00,582 --> 01:38:02,793
which is exactly what you
and I would both be doing

1564
01:38:02,959 --> 01:38:04,294
if I left here with you.

1565
01:38:04,461 --> 01:38:06,129
I'm not afraid of Crimson Dawn.

1566
01:38:06,296 --> 01:38:08,298
I can take care of myself.

1567
01:38:08,465 --> 01:38:09,800
You know,
I'm not the kid you knew

1568
01:38:09,883 --> 01:38:11,176
on Corellia anymore, Qi'ra.

1569
01:38:11,343 --> 01:38:12,469
- No?
- No.

1570
01:38:12,636 --> 01:38:13,678
Then who are you?

1571
01:38:14,596 --> 01:38:16,014
I'm an outlaw.

1572
01:38:17,933 --> 01:38:19,142
What? I'm not kidding.

1573
01:38:19,309 --> 01:38:20,394
Okay.

1574
01:38:21,186 --> 01:38:23,397
Okay, outlaw,
you can tell yourself that,

1575
01:38:23,563 --> 01:38:25,565
but I might be the only person
in the whole galaxy

1576
01:38:25,732 --> 01:38:27,067
who knows what you really are.

1577
01:38:27,234 --> 01:38:28,860
Yeah.

1578
01:38:29,152 --> 01:38:30,487
What's that?

1579
01:38:32,864 --> 01:38:34,574
You are the good guy.

1580
01:38:36,535 --> 01:38:39,204
I am not the good guy.

1581
01:38:39,371 --> 01:38:42,916
I am definitely not a good guy.

1582
01:38:43,291 --> 01:38:44,626
I'm a terrible person.

1583
01:38:45,085 --> 01:38:46,336
Hey!

1584
01:38:46,795 --> 01:38:48,255
They say when
the coaxium's refined,

1585
01:38:48,338 --> 01:38:49,756
we collect it up there.

1586
01:39:14,197 --> 01:39:16,199
So, I hear you make good brandy.

1587
01:39:19,870 --> 01:39:21,496
Beckett.

1588
01:39:46,104 --> 01:39:47,189
Don't.

1589
01:39:48,356 --> 01:39:50,859
You must've known
you'd see me again.

1590
01:39:51,026 --> 01:39:52,611
I was counting on it.

1591
01:39:52,777 --> 01:39:54,738
Just didn't plan on it
being so soon.

1592
01:39:55,906 --> 01:39:57,699
Of course now,
you've got a problem.

1593
01:39:57,866 --> 01:39:59,743
Big problem.

1594
01:40:03,455 --> 01:40:05,832
You happen to notice
that freighter down there?

1595
01:40:05,999 --> 01:40:07,751
You know what's on it?

1596
01:40:08,210 --> 01:40:09,920
About 30 hired guns.

1597
01:40:10,086 --> 01:40:11,922
All I gotta do
is give 'em the signal,

1598
01:40:12,005 --> 01:40:13,423
you're surrounded.

1599
01:40:29,731 --> 01:40:31,733
Sorry.
You do your thing.

1600
01:40:32,901 --> 01:40:35,278
By the time that coaxium
gets refined,

1601
01:40:35,445 --> 01:40:36,988
Crimson Dawn will be here,

1602
01:40:37,155 --> 01:40:38,865
so you go ahead and kill us.

1603
01:40:39,074 --> 01:40:40,283
They're gonna kill you.

1604
01:40:40,992 --> 01:40:42,285
Perhaps there's a compromise,

1605
01:40:42,452 --> 01:40:43,954
one that doesn't involve
so much killing.

1606
01:40:44,371 --> 01:40:45,789
They're marauders.

1607
01:40:46,373 --> 01:40:48,917
They don't care about anybody.

1608
01:40:49,751 --> 01:40:51,628
All they know how to do is kill.

1609
01:41:14,859 --> 01:41:16,319
I need a drink.

1610
01:41:16,903 --> 01:41:18,196
Bring them inside.

1611
01:41:30,542 --> 01:41:32,419
My mother once told me

1612
01:41:32,586 --> 01:41:33,920
about a band of mercenaries

1613
01:41:34,004 --> 01:41:35,630
that came to a peaceful planet.

1614
01:41:36,381 --> 01:41:39,467
They had a resource there
these men coveted,

1615
01:41:39,843 --> 01:41:41,261
so they took it.

1616
01:41:41,761 --> 01:41:44,639
They kept coming back,
taking more.

1617
01:41:45,390 --> 01:41:47,559
Until finally,
the people resisted.

1618
01:41:48,059 --> 01:41:49,686
When they returned
demanding their tribute,

1619
01:41:49,853 --> 01:41:52,897
the people shouted back
in one voice, "No more!"

1620
01:41:53,773 --> 01:41:55,900
The mercenaries didn't like
the sound of that,

1621
01:41:56,067 --> 01:41:57,444
so they cut off the tongue

1622
01:41:57,527 --> 01:42:00,447
of every last man,
woman, and child.

1623
01:42:01,281 --> 01:42:03,241
Do you know what
that pack of animals became?

1624
01:42:04,409 --> 01:42:05,410
Tell them.

1625
01:42:17,255 --> 01:42:19,507
Crimson Dawn and the rest of
the five Syndicates

1626
01:42:19,674 --> 01:42:21,134
have committed
unspeakable crimes

1627
01:42:21,217 --> 01:42:22,469
across the galaxy.

1628
01:42:23,553 --> 01:42:24,971
Says you.

1629
01:42:25,055 --> 01:42:26,056
No.

1630
01:42:26,139 --> 01:42:27,724
Says them.

1631
01:42:28,266 --> 01:42:30,393
Each of our worlds
has been brutalized

1632
01:42:30,477 --> 01:42:31,770
by the Syndicates.

1633
01:42:32,145 --> 01:42:33,647
Crimson Dawn
will use their profits

1634
01:42:33,730 --> 01:42:35,023
from the coaxium you stole

1635
01:42:35,190 --> 01:42:37,150
to tyrannize system after system

1636
01:42:37,317 --> 01:42:39,277
in league with the Empire.

1637
01:42:39,444 --> 01:42:41,321
And what would you use it for?

1638
01:42:42,280 --> 01:42:44,032
The same thing my mother
would have used it for

1639
01:42:44,199 --> 01:42:46,910
if she had survived
and still wore the mask.

1640
01:42:48,119 --> 01:42:49,245
To fight back.

1641
01:42:50,705 --> 01:42:52,749
We're not marauders.

1642
01:42:52,916 --> 01:42:54,668
We're allies

1643
01:42:55,418 --> 01:42:57,420
and the war has just begun.

1644
01:43:13,269 --> 01:43:16,439
You know we can't give
the coaxium to Dryden Vos.

1645
01:43:16,606 --> 01:43:18,566
Joining the cause, Han Solo?

1646
01:43:18,733 --> 01:43:20,985
Just trying
to make it out alive.

1647
01:43:21,152 --> 01:43:22,153
Got a plan?

1648
01:43:22,320 --> 01:43:23,530
Yeah, beginning of one.

1649
01:43:23,613 --> 01:43:24,614
Way to get our money

1650
01:43:24,781 --> 01:43:25,990
and get out from under the thumb

1651
01:43:26,074 --> 01:43:27,367
of Crimson Dawn
at the same time.

1652
01:43:27,534 --> 01:43:30,161
Maybe get your girlfriend back
while we're at it.

1653
01:43:30,995 --> 01:43:33,623
You don't tangle with Dryden.

1654
01:43:33,790 --> 01:43:37,001
Because unlike us,
he actually does travel

1655
01:43:37,168 --> 01:43:39,629
with hired guns,
his own private army.

1656
01:43:40,213 --> 01:43:41,715
So does Enfys.

1657
01:43:42,006 --> 01:43:44,259
Listen,
here's what I got so far.

1658
01:43:46,386 --> 01:43:48,471
What do you think
they're saying?

1659
01:43:51,766 --> 01:43:53,393
He's gonna try to help you.

1660
01:43:59,315 --> 01:44:00,734
I see.

1661
01:44:02,193 --> 01:44:05,780
Lot of ways it could go south,
and only one where it doesn't.

1662
01:44:05,947 --> 01:44:08,450
That's why I need my partner.

1663
01:44:12,579 --> 01:44:14,414
Not this time.

1664
01:44:14,748 --> 01:44:16,082
I'm leaving.

1665
01:44:16,249 --> 01:44:18,251
If you're smart,
you'll come with me.

1666
01:44:18,418 --> 01:44:20,628
I thought
you didn't believe in running.

1667
01:44:20,795 --> 01:44:23,214
I prefer it to dying.

1668
01:44:50,283 --> 01:44:52,952
If by some miracle
you make it out of here,

1669
01:44:53,119 --> 01:44:54,621
find me on Tatooine.

1670
01:44:55,413 --> 01:44:57,207
What's on Tatooine?

1671
01:44:57,373 --> 01:44:58,541
Heard about a job,

1672
01:44:58,625 --> 01:45:01,252
big shot gangster
putting together a crew.

1673
01:45:01,503 --> 01:45:03,171
That'll be the one.

1674
01:45:03,254 --> 01:45:04,255
The one?

1675
01:45:04,422 --> 01:45:06,216
My last score.

1676
01:45:06,674 --> 01:45:08,301
Yeah, I still got
some debts to pay

1677
01:45:08,384 --> 01:45:10,845
before I can head back
to Glee Anselm

1678
01:45:11,721 --> 01:45:13,723
and get into the valachord.

1679
01:45:46,965 --> 01:45:47,966
Welcome home.

1680
01:45:48,216 --> 01:45:49,968
He's waiting for you.

1681
01:45:50,134 --> 01:45:51,344
Thanks, Toht.

1682
01:45:52,971 --> 01:45:54,514
Weapons.

1683
01:45:54,681 --> 01:45:56,182
I didn't bring 'em.

1684
01:45:57,642 --> 01:45:59,018
They're fine.

1685
01:46:03,231 --> 01:46:05,233
We're gonna win.

1686
01:46:08,111 --> 01:46:09,571
It's not that kind of game, Han.

1687
01:46:11,656 --> 01:46:12,949
The object isn't to win.

1688
01:46:13,032 --> 01:46:15,118
It's just to stay in it
as long as you can.

1689
01:46:18,079 --> 01:46:19,539
You don't know everything.

1690
01:46:20,582 --> 01:46:21,791
No.

1691
01:46:24,085 --> 01:46:26,129
Just a bit more than you.

1692
01:46:34,429 --> 01:46:35,430
I knew it!

1693
01:46:36,431 --> 01:46:37,682
My men, they all said,

1694
01:46:37,765 --> 01:46:39,684
"There's no way
they pull this off."

1695
01:46:39,851 --> 01:46:41,227
"Qi'ra's not ready."
That's what they said,

1696
01:46:41,394 --> 01:46:43,730
but I had faith anyway.

1697
01:46:45,607 --> 01:46:46,733
Where's Beckett?

1698
01:46:46,900 --> 01:46:48,401
Beckett didn't make it.

1699
01:46:52,196 --> 01:46:53,197
Tell me.

1700
01:46:53,364 --> 01:46:55,867
Job took a bad turn on Kessel.

1701
01:46:56,034 --> 01:46:57,493
He died saving my life.

1702
01:46:57,952 --> 01:46:59,579
How are you holding up?
You all right?

1703
01:46:59,871 --> 01:47:00,872
I'm okay.

1704
01:47:01,039 --> 01:47:02,373
All right, good.

1705
01:47:02,790 --> 01:47:04,334
Colo claw fish, anyone?

1706
01:47:04,500 --> 01:47:05,752
- No. Thank you.
- No?

1707
01:47:05,919 --> 01:47:08,338
You know, whatever Beckett's
shortcomings may have been,

1708
01:47:08,421 --> 01:47:09,422
I always admired him.

1709
01:47:09,589 --> 01:47:11,132
He was a man of principles.

1710
01:47:11,299 --> 01:47:13,343
When he made a commitment,
he honored it

1711
01:47:13,593 --> 01:47:15,678
and I think we can
all take solace

1712
01:47:15,845 --> 01:47:18,389
in knowing how proud
he would've been

1713
01:47:18,556 --> 01:47:21,893
to see you here,
following his example.

1714
01:47:22,060 --> 01:47:23,811
Han and Chewbacca
behaved admirably.

1715
01:47:23,978 --> 01:47:24,979
They'll make reliable smugglers,

1716
01:47:25,063 --> 01:47:26,105
should we ever have the need

1717
01:47:26,272 --> 01:47:28,483
when they get their own ship.

1718
01:47:28,650 --> 01:47:30,860
Qi'ra.
Come here.

1719
01:47:32,695 --> 01:47:34,656
We'd really appreciate
the opportunity

1720
01:47:34,739 --> 01:47:35,949
to work for you again, sir.

1721
01:47:36,240 --> 01:47:37,659
I would've been inconsolable

1722
01:47:37,742 --> 01:47:39,619
if anything had
happened to you, my dear.

1723
01:47:40,828 --> 01:47:42,705
I have no one else in my life

1724
01:47:43,206 --> 01:47:46,000
that I trust in the way
that I trust you.

1725
01:47:49,671 --> 01:47:52,298
Well, I guess we'll just
take our payment

1726
01:47:52,382 --> 01:47:53,549
and get going.

1727
01:47:53,633 --> 01:47:54,634
I'm sure you've got
competitors to crush...

1728
01:47:54,717 --> 01:47:55,718
What?

1729
01:47:55,802 --> 01:47:57,345
...and black markets
to dominate.

1730
01:47:57,428 --> 01:47:59,639
Show me what
you've brought me first.

1731
01:48:00,306 --> 01:48:01,933
You want me to open it?

1732
01:48:02,433 --> 01:48:04,686
Yes, Han. I really do.

1733
01:48:31,129 --> 01:48:32,296
Bring me one.

1734
01:48:32,588 --> 01:48:35,258
I don't think
that's a good idea, Dryden.

1735
01:48:35,425 --> 01:48:37,343
It's very explosive stuff.

1736
01:48:37,885 --> 01:48:40,388
I never ask
for anything twice, Han.

1737
01:49:00,867 --> 01:49:02,535
Careful.

1738
01:49:06,164 --> 01:49:07,999
It's magnificent.

1739
01:49:08,750 --> 01:49:09,917
How'd you do it?

1740
01:49:10,001 --> 01:49:11,002
Wasn't easy.

1741
01:49:11,085 --> 01:49:12,420
No, I mean, how'd you do it?

1742
01:49:12,587 --> 01:49:14,547
It looks exactly
like the real thing.

1743
01:49:15,506 --> 01:49:17,300
That's
'cause it is the real thing.

1744
01:49:17,383 --> 01:49:18,384
Yes, and I'm saying

1745
01:49:18,551 --> 01:49:20,219
I would believe you.
It's that good.

1746
01:49:20,386 --> 01:49:22,263
But my associate already told me

1747
01:49:22,346 --> 01:49:24,807
about your plan to rob me
of my money

1748
01:49:24,974 --> 01:49:27,602
and give the real coaxium
to Enfys Nest.

1749
01:49:27,769 --> 01:49:29,479
Dryden, I don't know
what you're thinking

1750
01:49:29,645 --> 01:49:31,022
or what Qi'ra
may have told you...

1751
01:49:31,189 --> 01:49:33,316
No, not Qi'ra.
Not Qi'ra.

1752
01:49:33,566 --> 01:49:34,859
Qi'ra, it turns out

1753
01:49:35,026 --> 01:49:36,527
has a weak spot for you,

1754
01:49:36,611 --> 01:49:38,112
and we'll deal with that later.

1755
01:49:38,279 --> 01:49:42,116
No, I'm talking about
my other associate.

1756
01:49:42,283 --> 01:49:44,285
Can you come in
and join us, please?

1757
01:49:56,172 --> 01:49:59,300
I am sorry, kid.

1758
01:50:02,470 --> 01:50:03,846
Why?

1759
01:50:03,930 --> 01:50:04,931
Come on.

1760
01:50:05,014 --> 01:50:06,891
Don't look at me like that.

1761
01:50:07,058 --> 01:50:08,518
You weren't paying attention.

1762
01:50:08,601 --> 01:50:11,062
I told you,
"Don't trust anybody."

1763
01:50:11,896 --> 01:50:14,065
Am I wrong about that?

1764
01:50:18,236 --> 01:50:19,737
Back away from that.

1765
01:50:19,904 --> 01:50:21,864
Put your paws
where I can see 'em.

1766
01:50:22,031 --> 01:50:23,866
Check that lid.

1767
01:50:25,910 --> 01:50:27,120
Clever.

1768
01:50:27,328 --> 01:50:28,871
It's too late.

1769
01:50:29,038 --> 01:50:31,707
Coaxium's refined,
and Enfys has it.

1770
01:50:32,041 --> 01:50:33,960
Well, we figured that.

1771
01:50:48,182 --> 01:50:49,976
Drop your weapons.

1772
01:50:53,354 --> 01:50:56,190
It's over.
We got them.

1773
01:50:56,357 --> 01:50:57,692
And there we have it.

1774
01:50:57,859 --> 01:50:59,735
Excellent work,
Aemon, thank you.

1775
01:50:59,902 --> 01:51:01,445
Qi'ra, help me.

1776
01:51:03,906 --> 01:51:05,449
Tell me what to do.

1777
01:51:06,200 --> 01:51:07,702
What would you do

1778
01:51:07,869 --> 01:51:12,081
if the person you most trusted
in the world

1779
01:51:12,540 --> 01:51:14,000
betrayed you?

1780
01:51:16,919 --> 01:51:18,254
I would want to know why.

1781
01:51:20,631 --> 01:51:22,633
If it was a moment of weakness

1782
01:51:22,717 --> 01:51:23,718
or something else.

1783
01:51:23,885 --> 01:51:24,886
And then what?

1784
01:51:26,429 --> 01:51:29,307
And then,
I would ask that person

1785
01:51:29,473 --> 01:51:31,767
to prove their loyalty

1786
01:51:31,934 --> 01:51:35,897
by sacrificing
something they love.

1787
01:51:43,988 --> 01:51:46,199
I tried to warn you about her.

1788
01:51:46,365 --> 01:51:48,534
You know,
you're wrong about one thing.

1789
01:51:48,910 --> 01:51:49,911
What?

1790
01:51:50,203 --> 01:51:52,163
I was paying attention.

1791
01:51:52,330 --> 01:51:54,790
You told Chewie
people are predictable.

1792
01:51:57,335 --> 01:51:59,462
You're no exception.

1793
01:52:05,176 --> 01:52:06,177
It's empty.

1794
01:52:06,344 --> 01:52:07,637
The case is empty.

1795
01:52:07,845 --> 01:52:10,223
Aemon, what's going on?
What's happening there?

1796
01:52:10,389 --> 01:52:11,641
Aemon?

1797
01:52:11,807 --> 01:52:12,975
Talk to me.

1798
01:52:38,793 --> 01:52:41,712
I hope you didn't send
all your fancy enforcers

1799
01:52:41,879 --> 01:52:43,381
because that would leave you

1800
01:52:43,464 --> 01:52:45,633
a little shorthanded
around here.

1801
01:52:46,759 --> 01:52:47,760
So,

1802
01:52:48,469 --> 01:52:52,265
if that case is empty,
then the real coaxium...

1803
01:52:52,431 --> 01:52:54,308
Leaves here with one of us.

1804
01:52:59,397 --> 01:53:00,773
Beckett, what are you doing?

1805
01:53:00,856 --> 01:53:01,857
Thinking.

1806
01:53:02,024 --> 01:53:03,401
And I prefer to be the only one

1807
01:53:03,484 --> 01:53:05,027
holding a blaster
while I'm doing it.

1808
01:53:05,194 --> 01:53:06,570
Han, grab that coaxium,

1809
01:53:06,737 --> 01:53:07,989
put it in the case.

1810
01:53:08,155 --> 01:53:09,573
Big stuff,
you're coming with me.

1811
01:53:11,492 --> 01:53:12,743
Don't do this, Beckett.

1812
01:53:12,910 --> 01:53:14,662
- We had a deal.
- Yeah.

1813
01:53:14,745 --> 01:53:15,746
I'm sorry,

1814
01:53:15,830 --> 01:53:17,248
but I'm also an entrepreneur.

1815
01:53:17,415 --> 01:53:19,542
I mean, you of all people
understand that.

1816
01:53:20,001 --> 01:53:21,168
Come on, let's go.

1817
01:53:22,211 --> 01:53:24,088
You're making a huge mistake.

1818
01:53:24,255 --> 01:53:25,339
Won't be my first.

1819
01:53:25,506 --> 01:53:26,882
It's gonna be your last.

1820
01:53:27,174 --> 01:53:28,342
Maybe.

1821
01:53:29,302 --> 01:53:30,803
Why you gotta be so negative?

1822
01:53:43,482 --> 01:53:44,608
Han,

1823
01:53:44,775 --> 01:53:46,485
now's as good a time as any

1824
01:53:46,569 --> 01:53:48,279
to reevaluate our relationship.

1825
01:53:48,821 --> 01:53:49,864
How so?

1826
01:53:50,531 --> 01:53:51,991
I was just thinking,

1827
01:53:52,408 --> 01:53:55,286
why don't we join forces
and go get Beckett together?

1828
01:53:55,453 --> 01:53:58,748
That is a great idea.
Let's do it. You go first.

1829
01:53:59,707 --> 01:54:01,500
Han.

1830
01:54:28,319 --> 01:54:30,863
You can't win, Han,
and even if you could,

1831
01:54:30,946 --> 01:54:31,947
you'd spend the rest
of your life

1832
01:54:32,031 --> 01:54:33,032
looking over your shoulder.

1833
01:54:34,283 --> 01:54:35,284
You know what?

1834
01:54:36,285 --> 01:54:38,079
I'm kind of getting
used to the idea.

1835
01:54:45,669 --> 01:54:47,129
I'm sorry.

1836
01:54:47,296 --> 01:54:49,256
Han, she's done things that

1837
01:54:49,340 --> 01:54:52,009
you could never understand,
but I do.

1838
01:54:52,176 --> 01:54:54,095
I understand her completely.

1839
01:54:55,096 --> 01:54:57,264
Once you're a part
of Crimson Dawn,

1840
01:54:57,431 --> 01:54:58,808
you can't leave.

1841
01:54:59,183 --> 01:55:00,810
It's not true.

1842
01:55:00,976 --> 01:55:02,228
I know you.

1843
01:55:02,645 --> 01:55:04,647
It's what I was taught.

1844
01:55:04,814 --> 01:55:06,565
Find your opponent's weakness,

1845
01:55:06,732 --> 01:55:07,900
and use it,

1846
01:55:08,067 --> 01:55:10,152
and today...

1847
01:55:12,530 --> 01:55:13,823
I'm yours.

1848
01:55:39,765 --> 01:55:41,225
I had to.

1849
01:55:42,309 --> 01:55:44,437
Yeah.
No, I mean, you did...

1850
01:55:44,603 --> 01:55:46,522
You did.

1851
01:55:48,649 --> 01:55:50,651
Beckett and Chewbacca,
you have to go after them.

1852
01:55:50,818 --> 01:55:52,027
What are you gonna do?

1853
01:55:52,194 --> 01:55:54,697
Well, if we give all
the coaxium to Enfys,

1854
01:55:54,864 --> 01:55:57,700
we're gonna need something
to buy our ship with.

1855
01:56:11,338 --> 01:56:13,841
- Qi'ra...
- Go and save Chewbacca.

1856
01:56:14,008 --> 01:56:17,261
He needs you and you're
gonna need him, too.

1857
01:56:23,601 --> 01:56:24,602
Smile.

1858
01:56:27,271 --> 01:56:29,732
That's the word.

1859
01:56:29,899 --> 01:56:31,150
Whenever I imagined myself

1860
01:56:31,233 --> 01:56:33,360
off with you
on some adventure...

1861
01:56:34,403 --> 01:56:36,489
Always makes me smile.

1862
01:56:44,038 --> 01:56:46,081
Go. I'm right behind you.

1863
01:57:37,591 --> 01:57:38,801
Yes?

1864
01:57:39,051 --> 01:57:42,054
I regret to inform you
that Dryden Vos is dead,

1865
01:57:42,680 --> 01:57:44,390
murdered by the thief he hired

1866
01:57:44,473 --> 01:57:45,849
to steal the coaxium shipment,

1867
01:57:46,016 --> 01:57:47,351
his friend,

1868
01:57:47,518 --> 01:57:49,270
Tobias Beckett.

1869
01:57:49,436 --> 01:57:52,273
Is that so?

1870
01:57:52,439 --> 01:57:55,526
Where is the shipment now?

1871
01:57:55,693 --> 01:57:56,735
Gone.

1872
01:57:56,902 --> 01:57:57,903
Beckett took it.

1873
01:57:58,070 --> 01:58:00,489
Slaughtered the others.
I alone survived.

1874
01:58:03,659 --> 01:58:06,829
One man couldn't have
done this alone.

1875
01:58:07,580 --> 01:58:09,123
I wasn't there,

1876
01:58:09,290 --> 01:58:12,126
but if I had been, perhaps
I could have saved him.

1877
01:58:20,217 --> 01:58:23,721
Bring the ship and come to me
on Dathomir

1878
01:58:23,887 --> 01:58:25,723
and you and I will then decide

1879
01:58:25,806 --> 01:58:28,100
what to do about
the traitor, Beckett,

1880
01:58:28,267 --> 01:58:30,894
and his accomplices.

1881
01:58:33,063 --> 01:58:34,398
I'm on my way.

1882
01:58:36,775 --> 01:58:37,943
Qi'ra,

1883
01:58:38,110 --> 01:58:39,320
you and I

1884
01:58:39,486 --> 01:58:42,448
will be working
much more closely

1885
01:58:42,615 --> 01:58:44,575
from now on.

1886
01:59:14,605 --> 01:59:16,899
You're relentless.
I'll give you that.

1887
01:59:18,359 --> 01:59:20,653
Came as fast as I could, buddy.

1888
01:59:20,986 --> 01:59:22,404
Dryden dead?

1889
01:59:24,406 --> 01:59:26,241
Qi'ra kill him?

1890
01:59:28,035 --> 01:59:30,287
Still don't get it, do you, kid?

1891
01:59:30,621 --> 01:59:32,873
It was never about you.

1892
01:59:33,332 --> 01:59:35,084
She's a survivor.

1893
01:59:36,001 --> 01:59:37,544
You know what your problem is?

1894
01:59:37,711 --> 01:59:39,755
You think everybody's like you.

1895
01:59:40,422 --> 01:59:42,007
Not you, kid.

1896
01:59:42,174 --> 01:59:43,801
You're nothing like me.

1897
01:59:45,719 --> 01:59:47,137
I hope you're still
paying attention

1898
01:59:47,304 --> 01:59:49,348
because now I'm gonna tell you
the most important...

1899
02:00:04,363 --> 02:00:06,949
You made the smart move, kid.

1900
02:00:07,116 --> 02:00:08,325
For once.

1901
02:00:09,827 --> 02:00:11,453
I woulda killed you.

1902
02:00:19,169 --> 02:00:23,215
I really was gonna
learn to play that valachord.

1903
02:00:23,674 --> 02:00:25,092
I know.

1904
02:02:18,288 --> 02:02:19,540
That's it. It's all loaded.

1905
02:02:23,919 --> 02:02:25,254
Do you know what that really is?

1906
02:02:25,337 --> 02:02:26,380
Yeah.

1907
02:02:26,463 --> 02:02:29,299
About 60 million credits
worth of refined coaxium.

1908
02:02:29,466 --> 02:02:30,509
No.

1909
02:02:30,676 --> 02:02:32,928
It's the blood that brings
life to something new.

1910
02:02:33,136 --> 02:02:35,097
Yeah, what?

1911
02:02:35,305 --> 02:02:36,557
A rebellion.

1912
02:02:37,516 --> 02:02:39,393
You could come with us,
you know.

1913
02:02:39,560 --> 02:02:41,854
We need warriors
and leaders like you.

1914
02:02:48,443 --> 02:02:50,404
Maybe someday
you'll feel different.

1915
02:02:50,863 --> 02:02:53,115
Don't hold your breath, kid.

1916
02:03:07,963 --> 02:03:09,339
Don't lose that.

1917
02:03:21,101 --> 02:03:23,020
Very few people
have actually seen

1918
02:03:23,103 --> 02:03:24,563
the StarCave Nebula.

1919
02:03:24,730 --> 02:03:25,814
It's breathtaking.

1920
02:03:25,981 --> 02:03:27,482
Not unlike your eyes.

1921
02:03:27,649 --> 02:03:29,359
How much do you know about
intertwined celestial bodies?

1922
02:03:29,526 --> 02:03:31,737
Because I happen to be
something of an authority.

1923
02:03:32,946 --> 02:03:35,240
By the way...

1924
02:03:40,370 --> 02:03:41,955
Han!

1925
02:03:42,039 --> 02:03:43,040
You're alive!

1926
02:03:43,123 --> 02:03:44,207
Yeah, no thanks to you.

1927
02:03:44,374 --> 02:03:45,876
I should have Chewie
rip your arms off.

1928
02:03:46,043 --> 02:03:47,252
In fact, Chewie, do it.

1929
02:03:47,419 --> 02:03:48,837
Hey, Han!
We are friends.

1930
02:03:49,004 --> 02:03:50,505
You know that.
We're friends. All right?

1931
02:03:56,053 --> 02:03:57,679
Look at you.

1932
02:03:57,846 --> 02:03:59,222
Thought he was gonna
rip your arms off.

1933
02:03:59,389 --> 02:04:00,474
I knew you were kidding.

1934
02:04:00,557 --> 02:04:01,558
No, you didn't.

1935
02:04:01,642 --> 02:04:03,143
- So, where's my cut?
- Your cut?

1936
02:04:04,436 --> 02:04:06,605
No, I don't think so.
We barely made it out alive.

1937
02:04:06,772 --> 02:04:08,774
All we ended up with was that.

1938
02:04:10,734 --> 02:04:12,486
Figure it's worth about 10,000,

1939
02:04:12,569 --> 02:04:14,154
maybe enough for
a decent buy-in.

1940
02:04:16,114 --> 02:04:17,532
You want a rematch?

1941
02:04:18,867 --> 02:04:20,118
Why not?

1942
02:04:24,206 --> 02:04:26,041
You fold now,

1943
02:04:26,208 --> 02:04:27,376
you walk away with enough

1944
02:04:27,459 --> 02:04:29,628
to get yourself
your own little ship.

1945
02:04:29,795 --> 02:04:31,296
You call,

1946
02:04:32,130 --> 02:04:34,257
I'm gonna clean you out again.

1947
02:04:46,395 --> 02:04:47,688
I don't know, I'm feeling lucky.

1948
02:04:52,567 --> 02:04:54,820
You really have it bad
for the Falcon, don't you?

1949
02:04:54,987 --> 02:04:57,781
It's mutual, trust me.
She belongs with me.

1950
02:05:07,332 --> 02:05:09,793
You got everything
you need there, pal?

1951
02:05:19,594 --> 02:05:21,096
Not bad.

1952
02:05:21,596 --> 02:05:23,473
Not bad. You know,

1953
02:05:24,224 --> 02:05:27,561
if you'd only had
this little green sylop,

1954
02:05:28,437 --> 02:05:30,105
you would've beaten this.

1955
02:05:35,360 --> 02:05:38,530
Fair and square, baby.
Fair and square.

1956
02:05:49,374 --> 02:05:50,667
Beckett said he heard about this

1957
02:05:50,751 --> 02:05:52,961
very big gangster
putting together a job.

1958
02:05:53,795 --> 02:05:55,922
No, I'm telling ya,

1959
02:05:56,089 --> 02:05:57,090
it's gonna be great.

1960
02:05:57,257 --> 02:05:59,134
When have I ever
steered you wrong?

